Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone, welcome back to Munro Live. I'm Kevin, I'm here with Eric and we're here at the Tesla Semi rollout\N大家好，欢迎回到Munro Live。我是凯文，今天和埃里克一起在特斯拉半挂卡车发布现场。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.82,0:00:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,event for their ride and drive event,\N他们的试乘试驾活动。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.66,0:00:11.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,the factory tour, and uh hopefully a couple of conversations with the the program team.\N工厂参观，以及希望能与项目团队进行几场对话。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.08,0:00:13.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've been here for a little bit. It sounds like we're going\N我们已经在这儿一会儿了。听起来我们正要开始
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:16.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,to see get to see quite a bit, which we're pretty excited about.\N能看到不少东西，我们对此非常兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.26,0:00:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um obviously it's a long time coming, so we'll have\N嗯，显然这已经期待很久了，所以我们将会迎来
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.22,0:00:23.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,to see what they have to offer. So, thanks. We appreciate it.\N看看他们能提供什么。谢谢大家，我们很感激。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.88,0:00:52.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today everyone, what we're going to do is we'll explain a little bit the process behind stamping, how we go from\N今天，我们将为大家讲解一下冲压工艺的流程，以及我们是如何从原材料到成品的。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.66,0:00:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,this to that.\N从这个到那个。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.06,0:00:58.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,To the final product. Now,\N到最终产品。现在，
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.74,0:01:04.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's uh it's going to be very interesting. We have a video here which we made for you a little bit visually,\N这会非常有趣。我们这里有一段视频，是特意为您制作的，视觉效果上有些特别。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.70,0:01:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,so you can you you can refer to my words what I'm saying, okay? So, we have a steel of coil here and what we\N所以你可以参考我说的话，好吗？我们这里有钢卷，然后我们
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.42,0:01:14.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially do, we throw it onto this CTL, which is a cut-to-length line,\N本质上，我们把它放到这条剪切定长线上。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.42,0:01:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we cut those blanks each shape and form\N然后我们根据每种形状和样式裁剪那些空白部分
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.98,0:01:21.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need. You see it here. Once this stack of blanks is ready to go,\N这就是我们需要的。你看这里，一旦这叠空白材料准备就绪，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.14,0:01:24.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,we put it into a tandem line. You can see the\N我们把它放进串联线。你可以看到
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.74,0:01:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,tandem line in the way in the background where you have a couple of streets.\N背景中有一条并行的车道，旁边有几条街道。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.18,0:01:35.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tandem line is the heart and soul of any stamping operation and it's a beauty.\N连续线是任何冲压工艺的心脏和灵魂，真是美极了。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.86,0:01:41.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a very very sophisticated line, state-of-the-art technology.\N这是一条非常非常先进的生产线，代表了最顶尖的技术水平。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.46,0:01:45.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, having said that, how do we make it actually work and run?\N所以，话虽如此，我们该如何让它真正运行起来呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.06,0:01:48.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Synchronized, elegant way the way stamping operates.\N同步而优雅，冲压运作的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.64,0:01:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,This tandem line consists of five presses,\N这条双联生产线由五台压力机组成，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.38,0:01:55.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,which weigh up to 2,800 tons,\N重量高达2800吨的
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.95,0:02:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is roughly 1,400 Model Ys.\N相当于大约1400辆Model Y。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.34,0:02:06.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are up to that. So, um but it's and we move hundreds of tons every second.\N我们已经做到这一点了。所以，嗯，我们每秒都在搬运数百吨。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.02,0:02:10.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we do this? We have up to 600 sensors installed in this line.\N我们怎么做？这条产线上最多安装了600个传感器。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.16,0:02:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,They all talk to each other. Every stroke signals\N它们彼此互通。每一次触控都传递信号。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.74,0:02:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,talk to each other in milliseconds. And all the 600 sensors, they have to say yes before anything moves.\N它们之间要在毫秒级别内通信，而且所有600个传感器必须全部确认后，系统才能动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.58,0:02:27.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we have also job data. Every part that you see, final part, has to 7,000 to 8,000 job data behind it. You\N此外，我们还有工作数据。你看到的每一个最终零件，背后都有七千到八千条工作数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.86,0:02:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,change one there, you change the part.\N改一个，整个部件就变了。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.26,0:02:35.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, two things that we do very different than any Tesla plant in the world. One is the handshake.\N现在，有两件事是我们与世界上任何一家特斯拉工厂都不同的。一是握手。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.78,0:02:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I call it the kiss.\N我称之为亲吻。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.38,0:02:40.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go open the oil again. It's the automation how we hand over the parts when\N打开油箱再试一次，是自动化系统在交接零件时出了问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.96,0:02:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have an idle station. And the other one is the in-die clinching. We\N我们有一个闲置的工位，另一个是芯片内的铆接。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.86,0:02:53.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,attach the fasteners in our stamping process inside the We don't need a lot of floor space. It's one machine, one\N在我们的冲压工艺中安装紧固件，我们不需要太多占地面积，只用一台机器即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.34,0:02:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,footprint. No more stud cells,\N占地面积。不再需要机架机柜，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.30,0:03:00.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,no more nut cells. Now,\N不再有螺母工位了。现在，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.78,0:03:01.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Keith, tell me what about those dies?\N凯斯，那些晶粒怎么样了？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.40,0:03:05.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good afternoon. My name's Keith Dworak.\N下午好，我叫基思·德沃拉克。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.46,0:03:08.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the staff tooling guy engineer for sub assembly here.\N我是这里子组件的专职工具工程人员。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.50,0:03:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once we get the blanks while they're in his group, they come into our between three or five processes they go\N一旦我们拿到空白样本，他们还在他组里的时候，这些样本就会进入我们的流程，在三到五个步骤中进行处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.46,0:03:18.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,into the press. Each process does something different.\N进入新闻界。每个流程都有不同的作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.19,0:03:23.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes in On the first one is form, then it will trim,\N首先输入形状，然后进行修剪，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.30,0:03:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,pierce, re-strike, and then put out. We have two open up here. This one here is a trim die over to my right. Three.\N刺穿、再击打，然后收手。这里有两个空位。这个在我右边的是一个修整的骰子。三。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.46,0:03:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And over here is four. This is a the re-strike here and flange. Once it goes through there,\N这边是四。这是重新定位的销钉和法兰。一旦穿过那里，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.50,0:03:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,it comes to the end of line where our quality department will take and put it on the static fixture here.\N到了生产线末端，我们的质检部门会将其固定在这个静止夹具上。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.26,0:03:44.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a series of pins and gauges that go on here to\N这里有一系列的销钉和量规需要安装。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.68,0:03:49.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,ensure that every part is trimmed the same, pierced the same,\N确保每个部件的修剪和穿孔都一致。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.58,0:03:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're all the same. Once that goes together, it's a beautiful thing. We make trucks. However, we're not done yet\N它们都是一样的。一旦组合起来，就非常美妙。我们制造卡车，但还没结束。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.82,0:03:59.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we want to make sure that y'all get you the\N因为我们想确保你们能顺利拿到
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.55,0:04:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,best part quality that you can. So, we send each one\N你能达到的最佳零件质量。所以，我们会对每一个进行处理
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.74,0:04:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,into a scanner system that you see here.\N变成你在这里看到的扫描系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.42,0:04:10.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has the data in a computerized automated design.\N它拥有计算机化自动设计的数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.86,0:04:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,You take that data with what we get from here and it shows there. If it's green,\N你把这里获取的数据与这些数据结合，就能在那儿看到结果。如果显示为绿色，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.14,0:04:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's beautiful. That's what we shoot for.\N太美了，这正是我们追求的目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.58,0:04:20.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we get all the time.\N这就是我们一直得到的结果。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.18,0:04:23.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I would be remiss if I didn't say that everything that you're\N呃，如果我不说，你们所看到的一切
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.55,0:04:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,about to see as you go through here has come through our\N接下来您将看到的，都是我们这边传过来的
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.90,0:04:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,line. We do 62 part numbers going through here.\N这里共有62个零部件在流转。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.18,0:04:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's hundreds of parts that you can see as you're surrounded here.\N这里你能看到数百个部件，周围全是。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.30,0:04:35.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Each one of them, the highest world-class quality we can\N它们每一个都达到了我们所能达到的最高世界级品质。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.79,0:04:40.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,possibly produce at the quickest, most efficient way possible.\N以最快、最高效的方式生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.06,0:04:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, Tesla's doing a lot of in-house stamping. From what we saw uh there and what was presented, it looks\N显然，特斯拉正在大量进行内部冲压。从我们所见以及展示的内容来看，看起来
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.86,0:04:52.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,like they essentially have a single kind of tandem line there for uh for stamping, blanking, and all the the\N它们实际上在那里只有一条用于冲压、剪切等工序的单一类型串联生产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.14,0:04:53.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,subsequent operations and trimming.\N后续操作和修整。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.94,0:04:59.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I didn't see any other stations like that. So, um when we kind of walked up into the station where they briefed, we\N我没看到其他类似的工位。所以，嗯，当我们走到他们介绍的那个工位时，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.46,0:05:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,are flanked on every side on each side, I should say,\N每一边都受到包围，这么说比较准确。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.70,0:05:09.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,um by a ton of essentially like very densely packed stampings. So, it suggests to me, based on what we could\N嗯，就像大量非常密集的冲压件堆在一起。所以，根据我们能了解到的情况，这暗示了我……
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.38,0:05:10.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,see here, that they've got not a ton of presses running um\N看这里，他们并没有太多压机在运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.96,0:05:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and given the volume of 50,000 units, it kind of makes sense\N考虑到5万单位的规模，这倒是说得通。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.50,0:05:22.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,that they're going to run bankable parts, swap out tools, batch build another set of parts, and then continue\N他们将运行可盈利的部件，更换工具，批量生产另一批部件，然后继续。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.18,0:05:23.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,that process um meeting essentially like I said, bank building,\N那个过程，嗯，基本上就像我说的，银行建设。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.43,0:05:27.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,building all that inventory up, and then keeping their\N积累所有这些库存，然后持续保持
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.38,0:05:32.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially presses running um and highly utilized uh essentially through the entire process. So, just one thing I\N本质上是全程运行且高度利用的，所以只有一件事我想说
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.34,0:05:34.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,wanted to kind of point out um when we're going through the stamping uh aspect\N想稍微指出一下，当我们谈到冲压这一环节时
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.91,0:05:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,of it cuz literally as we were walking into the building, it took a\N因为就在我们走进大楼的时候，它真的花了
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.42,0:05:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,little bit to get to there. It's off to the left-hand side and just the entire left-hand side is essentially just\N稍微往左一点，整个左侧基本上就是
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.14,0:05:45.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,stacked uh stamped parts, you know,\N堆叠的、压印好的零件，你知道的
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.50,0:05:48.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,ready for assembly. And then the far right side was essentially assembly cells and\N准备进行组装。而最右侧基本上是组装工位。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.76,0:05:52.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,the powder coating cells as well. And a key point there, we'll talk\N粉末喷涂车间也是如此。其中关键的一点，我们稍后会讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.54,0:05:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit more about it, but we walked right in.\N再多说一点，但我们直接就进去了。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.66,0:05:57.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,They obviously weren't running anything,\N他们显然什么都没在运行，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.74,0:06:01.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,but there's no hazmat areas or anything like that. We walked right into the line. The powder coating cells were off\N但这里没有危险品区域之类的，我们直接就走进了生产线。粉末喷涂工位是关闭的。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.58,0:06:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the right-hand side. Just a big advantage of the uh powder coating over your kind of traditional liquid paint cells\N右侧。粉末涂层相比传统液态涂料具有明显优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.86,0:06:12.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,um with respect to kind of what you need to do to maintain um a paint shop like that.\N关于维持这样一个喷漆车间，你具体需要做些什么，这方面我得说清楚。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.86,0:06:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the manufacturing engineer for uh top cover and the visual battery factors. Uh the part that I simply use\N我是顶盖和视觉电池组件的制造工程师，我负责的这个部件非常简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.18,0:06:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,here on my left as enclosure and then the one you see on the right as top cover. They assemble together to form\N左边是外壳，右边是顶盖。它们组装在一起形成
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.70,0:06:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh high voltage structural housing or uh battery assembly.\N高压结构外壳或电池组装配。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.82,0:06:33.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as you can see this assembly, we spend a good time\N所以，正如你们所见，这个组装过程我们花了相当长的时间
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.94,0:06:39.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,to develop uh an optimal number of components so that we\N以确定最优的组件数量，使我们
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.26,0:06:41.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,can achieve the best uh kilowatt per hour per uh per\N每千瓦时每小时可达到最佳效能
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.50,0:06:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,weight of each each assemblies. Uh just to put it into\N每个组件的重量。呃，简单来说就是
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.74,0:06:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,perspective, uh as you can see this is the size of\N视角上，你看，这是尺寸
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.46,0:06:55.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,our residential bathtub and then the weight is similar to a\N我们的家用浴缸，然后重量与一个
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.46,0:06:57.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,commercial refrigerator. Um so, we like this is the uh enclosure\N商用冰箱。嗯，所以我们喜欢这个外壳
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.64,0:07:01.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and the top cover lines as well. We We have more\N还有顶部的导流板。我们还有更多
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.98,0:07:08.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,than 100 robots and then we use advanced automation uh technology and then different fixture and strategies as well\N超过100台机器人，然后我们使用先进的自动化技术，以及不同的夹具和策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.42,0:07:15.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then different uh assembly technologies uh which my friend Selo will explain later about the processes.\N然后是不同的组装技术，稍后我的朋友塞洛会详细讲解这些工艺。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.54,0:07:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um to keep the part to the highest quality standard, we are going we are using 100% inline inspection and then\N为了确保零部件达到最高质量标准，我们将采用100%的在线检测。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.98,0:07:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,vision-assisted dimensional uh tolerance uh offset as well. Um so,\N视觉辅助的尺寸公差和偏移量也一并考虑。嗯，所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.58,0:07:34.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,once the line is complete in in our line, it will go to a downstream application which is e-coat process.\N线路完成后，将进入下游应用，即电泳涂装工序。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.74,0:07:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,After the e-coat, it goes to high voltage battery assembly line\N电泳漆处理后，它将进入高压电池组装线。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.70,0:07:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,which you will see later in your tour. I'll give\N稍后参观时你会看到。我来介绍
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.18,0:07:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,my I'll give it to my friend Cello.\N我把它给我朋友切洛。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.70,0:07:51.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Evenet. Welcome everybody. My name is Cello. I've been with Tesla since 3 years. I'm responsible for\N谢谢，埃文。欢迎大家。我叫塞洛，三年前加入特斯拉，负责
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.26,0:07:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,joining and process engineering.\N加入与工艺工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.30,0:07:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.06,0:07:57.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,to put them together, we use three different joining technologies for the battery\N为了将它们组合在一起，我们采用了三种不同的连接技术来连接电池。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.16,0:08:01.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,top cover and for the battery enclosure, we use six different joining\N顶盖和电池舱体部分，我们采用了六种不同的连接方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.30,0:08:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,technologies. In total, we have seven different joining technologies. For example, at the battery top cover, you\N技术。总共，我们采用了七种不同的连接技术。例如，在电池顶盖上，您
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.42,0:08:10.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,can see here the gold line, it's a laser brazing seam.\N可以看到，这条金色的线是激光钎焊缝。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.28,0:08:15.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use laser brazing, we have resistance spot welds, we have\N我们使用激光钎焊，还有电阻点焊。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.58,0:08:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesives. On the battery enclosure side, we have mark welds, we have resistance spot welds as well,\N结构胶。在电池包外壳一侧，我们有激光焊点，也有电阻点焊。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.10,0:08:24.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesives, drawn arc welds.\N结构胶粘剂，电弧焊缝。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.42,0:08:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do have projection welding. We do also multi-material mix between steel and aluminum. That's the reason we also\N我们确实有投影焊，也实现了钢与铝的多材料混合，这也是我们如此做的原因
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.62,0:08:37.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,use self-piercing rivets. Um just to get an idea how many spot welds we have here, for long range truck, we have we\N使用自冲铆钉。嗯，大致了解一下，这款长续航卡车这里我们有多少个点焊点。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.26,0:08:42.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,need three battery structures. That means per battery structure, we have 1,000 spot welds.\N需要三个电池结构，这意味着每个电池结构有1000个点焊。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.54,0:08:46.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with three battery structures, we would be at 3,000 spot welds.\N有了三个电池结构，我们将需要3000个点焊。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.04,0:08:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compared to the cab from the Semi, we would have\N与半挂车驾驶室相比，我们的设计将会
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.70,0:08:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,the we would have the 2,800 spot welds.\N我们将拥有2800个点焊。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.70,0:08:56.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we do have more spot welds at the battery systems than at the entire cab.\N因此，电池系统上的点焊数量比整个驾驶室还多。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.46,0:09:05.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the next thing we saw was essentially the battery tray itself. Um kind of off the side, it's it's it's\N接下来我们看到的基本上就是电池托盘本身。嗯，有点偏在侧面，它是……
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.06,0:09:08.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,primarily steel. As you can kind of see here off to the right, a series of stampings.\N主要是钢制的。你可以看到右边有一系列冲压件。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.82,0:09:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um each one of their modules essentially slot in horizontally.\N它们每个模块基本上都是横向插入的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.98,0:09:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We did get to see um a battery that was deleted. We could\N我们确实看到一个被删除的电池。我们能
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.98,0:09:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,see inside.\N看看里面。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.06,0:09:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we were asked not to film that. Um I don't want to speak\N呃，我们被要求不要拍那段。呃，我不想说
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.62,0:09:23.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,too much about it and kind of respect that, but at a high\N对这件事太过关注，某种程度上确实值得尊重，但话说回来，还是太高了。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.14,0:09:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,level, it reminded me a lot of essentially an early Model S pack. Um the big thing that I took away from that\N这一级让我想起了早期的Model S电池组。我从中得到的最大感受是
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.18,0:09:32.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,is, like everything with the Semi truck,\N就像所有半挂卡车一样，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.66,0:09:34.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,serviceability. So, as you know, as we have seen the\N可服务性。因此，正如大家所知，正如我们所见的那样，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.01,0:09:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,progression essentially from uh the use of aluminum extrusions,\N本质上是从使用铝型材开始的进展，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.86,0:09:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,castings into and their battery packs,\N铸件及其电池组，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.14,0:09:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,then the transition essentially with your later Model Y's, Model 3's and such to the stamp packs. We essentially\N然后，您后续的 Model Y、Model 3 等车型将逐步过渡到冲压件包。我们基本上
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.14,0:09:51.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tesla's one of the few companies we've seen numerous generations of packs being uh,\N特斯拉是少数我们见过多代电池包迭代的公司之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.89,0:09:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,iterated and put into the marketplace. Um, so seeing a primarily\N迭代后投入市场。嗯，看到一个主要面向市场的例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.74,0:09:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,steel pack here is exactly what I expected to see. Um, I was a little um,\N这里的钢包正是我所期待看到的。呃，我有点……
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.98,0:10:02.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,surprised to see and I don't want to say lack of integration,\N没想到会看到，我不想说缺乏整合，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.20,0:10:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but when I when we saw inside that essentially um, it's\N但当我们真正看到里面时，基本上可以说，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.50,0:10:12.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,clear that they um, balanced that decision out favoring serviceability and long service life\N清楚地表明，他们权衡了这一决策，更倾向于可维护性和长期使用寿命。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.30,0:10:13.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the pack and the modules itself.\N以及模块本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.74,0:10:17.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it looked like everything that we saw that was loaded into here,\N所以，看起来我们看到的所有加载到这里的内容都……
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.48,0:10:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the cassettes of uh, 4680s um, was serviceable.\N4680 型电池组的磁带，嗯，还算可用。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.06,0:10:22.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,But as you can kind of look through here and I\N但你可以大致看看这里，我
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.13,0:10:25.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,was having a brief conversation with Jordan, he didn't necessarily know\N正跟乔丹简短聊了几句，他未必清楚
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.82,0:10:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,where the orientation and frankly even when I first walked in, I kind of thought this was longitudinally oriented\N方向上，坦白说，我刚进来的时候，还以为它是纵向排列的
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.06,0:10:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,and this was looking at from the side of the vehicle uh,\N从车辆侧面观察时，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.30,0:10:36.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,just based off of the structure that is present on the side of\N仅根据侧边存在的结构
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.06,0:10:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,the pack. So, they have like a dedicated section on the upper part which is supporting the mounting to the pack to\N电池组。所以它们在上部有一个专用区域，用于支撑电池组的安装。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.86,0:10:44.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,the frame and then they have essentially some outriggers on the lower portion.\N框架下方还装有一些伸缩支架。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.62,0:10:48.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but that's actually it's transversely mounted.\N嗯，但实际上它是横向安装的。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.78,0:10:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is actually these cutouts here are for the main frame rail sections and essentially they have cross members\N实际上，这些开孔是用于主框架横梁部分的，它们本质上带有横梁。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.50,0:10:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,running across the top um, and the side and they kind of fills the entire cavity of um,\N从顶部横向延伸，再到侧面，几乎填满了整个腔体。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.78,0:11:04.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,on a traditional truck where you would essentially see fuel tanks,\N在传统卡车上，你基本上会看到燃油箱，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.62,0:11:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,um, exhaust aftertreatment, storage boxes and things of that nature. On the Tesla Semi, it's the batteries\N嗯，废气后处理装置、储物箱之类的。在特斯拉半挂车上，就是电池。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.42,0:11:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially running um, cross car all the way out to probably if I had to guess maybe a\N基本上是跨车运行，一直延伸到可能，如果非要猜的话，大概
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.66,0:11:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,a 400 3 to say 500 mm threshold of your outer aero skirts.\N400 3 的外侧空气动力学裙边阈值为 500 毫米。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.82,0:11:23.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you essentially get to um, a series of uh,\N然后你基本上就得到一系列的，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.88,0:11:29.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,structures that they build off this. Um, but really when you look\N他们基于此构建的结构。嗯，但真正来看，当你深入观察时
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.06,0:11:32.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,at it, I mean it looks a lot like essentially a a frame on a truck.\N我意思是，它看起来基本上就像卡车上的一个框架。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.16,0:11:36.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I fully expected that this was actually, you know, or\N我本来完全预料到，这实际上……你知道的，或者
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.42,0:11:38.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,oriented to the front and and and interfacing with the cradle\N朝前并对接到支架上
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.16,0:11:41.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and whatever they were doing for the rear drive modules.\N以及他们对后轮驱动模块所做的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.42,0:11:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I felt a little silly when I finally saw them oriented in vehicle and and saw that. Um\N说实话，当我终于看到它们在车里朝向正确位置时，感觉有点傻。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.78,0:11:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, you know, again, lots of use of castings, excuse me,\N不过，你知道的，再次强调，大量使用了铸件，抱歉。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.10,0:11:56.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um of stampings throughout this. Small use of essentially redundant uh castings here\N整个过程中冲压件的总用量。这里几乎用到了冗余的铸件。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.10,0:11:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,for all the um outer nodes. There's a unique one for the inner provisions.\N对于所有外部节点，都有一个对应的外层节点；而内部节点则有其唯一的内层节点。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.22,0:12:06.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,They all look like they can slip a little bit in Z. Um these lower um weldments here, I was a\N它们看起来在 Z 方向上都有一点点松动。这些下方的焊件，我之前
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.58,0:12:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,little prior to little surprised to see that they were essentially a big weldment. A lot of MIG welding going on\N就在之前，我还真没想到他们会是这么一大块焊接件，现场MIG焊机正在大量作业。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.66,0:12:13.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,here. We don't see MIG welding, I think,\N这里。我们看不到MIG焊接，我想。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.06,0:12:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,anywhere else in the plant um besides here. So, makes me kind of wonder where this is being done based off of\N工厂的其他地方，除了这里。所以，我有点好奇，这到底是哪里在做。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.66,0:12:22.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,everything else we saw there. It wouldn't surprise me to see these turn into a casting in the future, but there\N我们看到的其他东西，未来它们可能会变成铸造件，这并不让我感到意外，但这里
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.58,0:12:24.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,might be a very deliberate reason why they are doing this.\N这背后可能有非常明确的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.59,0:12:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I just couldn't tell from just looking at it. But, you\N呃，我光看一眼还真分辨不出来。不过，你
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.82,0:12:31.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,can kind of see there's an internal bulkhead here.\N可以看到这里有一道内部隔板。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.66,0:12:34.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, um where this external mounting interface here is, what uh is here,\N所以，呃，这个外部安装接口在这里，呃，这里是什么，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.32,0:12:38.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,what complements this is essentially a large cast U-shape\N这背后实际上是一组大型U形结构的补充
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.42,0:12:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,bulkhead. You can see a little bit of this.\N舱壁。你能看到一点这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.46,0:12:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We didn't have a better picture of this.\N我们之前没有更清晰的图像。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.22,0:12:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll try and get one uh or ask some friends if we can get a better shot um from inside the pack itself. And then\N我们试试看能不能弄到一个，或者问问朋友，看能不能从队伍内部拍到更好的画面。然后
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.98,0:12:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,that is complemented by two stampings that provide that section that runs across. And this complements this area\N这由两个冲压件补充，它们提供了贯穿该区域的结构。这正好与该区域相匹配。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.94,0:13:00.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,here on the top where the frames are running through. So, realistically, all those loads, if there was an impact,\N这里上方，画面帧正在通过。因此，实际上，如果发生撞击，所有这些负载都会受到影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.06,0:13:02.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,whether it's from the front, the rear,\N无论是从前方还是后方
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.06,0:13:04.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,or anything like that, um these these packs are daisy chained together.\N或者类似的东西，嗯，这些模块是串联在一起的。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.65,0:13:07.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,This would run up if this was a four-pack up\N如果是四包的话，这就会往上走
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.50,0:13:10.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,into the chassis and then your subsequent mid and uh rear packs are also\N装入底盘后，你后续的中段和后段电池包也是一样
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.35,0:13:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of daisy chained off this in a big structural bulkhead. This made me\N像一大块结构隔板上串联起来的雏菊一样。这让我
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.90,0:13:22.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,really think of essentially modern aircraft. Have you ever seen how like an F-18 and F-35 are actually really like\N真的得想想现代飞机。你有没有仔细看过F-18和F-35，它们其实非常相似
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.50,0:13:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,an F-14 big huge titanium bulkhead um you know, within it. And actually a pretty interesting process. That's why\N一个F-14大型钛合金隔板，就在里面。实际上，这个工艺还挺有意思的。这就是原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.26,0:13:30.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,they scrapped them all um after they were decommissioned. But, overall,\N它们在退役后全部被拆除了。但总的来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.90,0:13:38.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,exactly kind of what we expected to see is um a series of stampings and a low-cost, you know, kind of strategy for\N正是我们预期看到的，一系列冲压件，以及一种低成本、类似的战略。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.86,0:13:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,their battery pack itself.\N它们的电池组本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.58,0:13:43.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to main line. Uh it's really exciting to share with you\N欢迎来到主线。真的很激动能与大家分享。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.64,0:13:47.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,all the final assembly of the Semi cabin, which is the\N所有半挂车车厢的最终组装，也就是
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.74,0:13:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the trail of the Semi.\N半导体的踪迹。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.78,0:13:54.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I'm Carlos as the process engineer for this body line.\N我是卡洛斯，负责这条车身生产线的工艺工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.54,0:13:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm Shreya Gorey. I'm the process engineering technician for body in white.\N我是什雷亚·戈雷，我是车身车间的工艺工程技术人员。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.94,0:14:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, here at the frame station, we put our main cabin together. We have our\N所以，在这个机架站，我们把主舱体组装在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.22,0:14:09.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,body side left, body side right, and underbody that come together.\N车身左侧、车身右侧和底盘部分组合而成。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.45,0:14:13.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're closed together, and then we have our\N它们紧紧闭合在一起，然后我们有
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.50,0:14:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,roof that comes on as the cherry on the top. So, we weld our\N屋顶就像锦上添花。因此，我们焊接我们的
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.50,0:14:23.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,cabin together. We also have two important joining technologies here.\N我们还在这里采用了两种重要的连接技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.78,0:14:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have resistance spot welding and\N我们有电阻点焊和
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.42,0:14:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,structural adhesive that is used to put this cabin together.\N用于组装这个舱体的结构胶。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.94,0:14:39.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once we put the cabin together, we send it to our robotic vision inspection system. From there, it goes to our\N组装完舱体后，我们会将其送往机器人视觉检测系统。之后，它会进入我们的下一个工序。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.10,0:14:45.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,end-of-line station, where we do our final uh quality checks before it goes to final assembly.\N下线检测站，在这里我们进行最终的质量检查，然后再进入最终组装。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.74,0:14:48.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next thing we saw was essentially the body in white.\N我们看到的下一件东西基本上就是白色的躯体。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.86,0:14:54.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, they didn't talk too much about this, but as you can kind of see, it's primarily all aluminum. I don't know if\N所以他们没怎么多谈这个，但你大概能看出，主要是铝制的。我不太知道
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.10,0:14:56.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's numerous grades. What we kind of saw on the inner A-pillar here,\N这里有很多不同的等级。我们在这根内A柱上看到的情况是，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.50,0:14:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,more specifically in that picture there, you\N更具体地说，那张图片里的那个
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.22,0:15:05.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,can kind of see um it's a slightly different hue. It might be a different grade, but uh there was nothing about\N看起来有点不一样，色调似乎有些不同，可能是不同等级的，但没什么特别的。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.70,0:15:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh the processing of coils as they kind of came in, where they talked about anything about surface treatments or\N嗯，关于线圈进入时的处理，他们有没有提到任何表面处理方面的问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.94,0:15:12.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,different grades being used in the plant. Um so, it could just be excuse me,\N工厂里使用了不同等级的材料。呃，所以可能只是抱歉，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.75,0:15:16.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,the light being thrown a particular way off of how\N光线以某种特定方式反射出来
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.18,0:15:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,this was illuminated, or it could be a different grade. Um but, primarily,\N这可能是被照亮的，也可能是不同等级的。嗯，但主要是……
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.17,0:15:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,um all large stampings, and and can kind of\N嗯，大型冲压件，还有那种
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.70,0:15:28.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,see through these These these aren't really being kicked together. Big stamping, big aperture piercing here\N看穿这些，这些其实并没有真正被压在一起。这里的大冲压、大孔径穿刺
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.02,0:15:30.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and relatively limited use of castings.\N以及相对有限的铸件使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.10,0:15:31.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.74,0:15:34.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,on the front upper A-pillar and the front header here,\N前挡风玻璃上方A柱和前顶棚这里，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.05,0:15:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's a unit casting here or a nodal casting and same thing on the other side.\N这里有一个单元铸造，或者说是节点铸造，另一边也是一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.90,0:15:44.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in the front of the vehicle here on this kind of horse collar structure,\N然后在这辆车辆前方，这种类似马轭的结构上，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.10,0:15:48.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,so the floor is here as it comes across. This is kind of a\N所以地板在这里，随着它延伸过来。这有点像
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.54,0:15:53.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,an underfloor cab rail. The face of that running across the lower portion of the dash pad,\N地板下的电缆导轨。其表面贯穿仪表板下部区域，
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.38,0:16:00.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's all cast, it's a single piece and we have steel crush cans themselves there. I don't think I saw any other\N这就是铸件，是单一整体，我们还有钢制压碎罐。我想我没看到别的。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.22,0:16:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,steel parts that were e-coated. They typically do this for corrosion.\N经过电泳涂装的钢制零件，通常这样做是为了防锈。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.78,0:16:06.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,There could be some essentially in seat mounts or restraint mounts like\N座椅或安全带支架中可能存在一些基本结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.69,0:16:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,tap it plates elsewhere within the vehicle and they would essentially be\N敲击车辆其他位置的板件，它们基本上会
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.26,0:16:14.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,e-coated like that as well and then captivated somewhere else within the vehicle.\N也像这样进行了电泳涂层，然后在车辆的其他位置被吸附。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.81,0:16:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I didn't see any other steel there. Again, in general we were\N但我没看到别的钢材。总的来说，我们也没看到
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.66,0:16:22.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,we were moved along pretty quickly through each one of these stations just given the number of people that were\N我们被迅速带过每一个站点，毕竟人太多了。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.54,0:16:23.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,coming through after us.\N跟在我们后面来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.62,0:16:26.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but high-level,\N但总的来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.74,0:16:29.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, there's when I look at this a little bit smoother\N你知道，当我稍微仔细看这个时，感觉更顺滑了
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.21,0:16:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,load paths than most trucks. You have a very forward seating\N比大多数卡车的载重路径更优。你的座椅位置非常靠前。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.30,0:16:40.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,position. The cab wraps around you quite a bit. So, essentially the seating the seat is here,\N位置。驾驶舱会环绕你相当多。所以，本质上座椅在这里，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.54,0:16:46.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but unlike most vehicles, this kind of balances a little bit of essentially cab over features and your kind of\N但与大多数车辆不同，这种车型在一定程度上融合了驾驶室前置的特性。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.50,0:16:53.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,traditional, you know, engine out front cab behind orientation, but you get essentially body structure that wraps\N传统的布局，发动机在前，驾驶室在后，但你实际上得到的是一个包裹式的车身结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.10,0:16:54.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,around you with the hinge pillar on more conventional trucks would be\N在普通卡车身上，铰接支柱的位置会更靠后
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.51,0:16:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,much closer to where you would expect to see it as\N更接近你预期的位置
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.38,0:17:03.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,you open the door, get right into the seat. Where here essentially you have essentially the door ring the and the\N你打开车门，直接坐进驾驶座。这里实际上就是车门铃和……
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.18,0:17:05.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,hinge pillar being one here.\N铰链支柱，这里就是一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.94,0:17:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And essentially that's all fixed.\N基本上，这都已修复完毕。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.42,0:17:12.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nothing there moves. Your window regulator, all that stuff goes to a very fixed point on the body.\N那里没有任何部件移动。你的车窗升降器，所有这些部件都连接到车身上的一个固定点。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.06,0:17:15.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, very different than what we typically see and frankly I think you\N所以，与我们通常看到的情况非常不同，坦白说，我觉得你
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.60,0:17:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,can really tell that you know, this is a a Semi truck that's\N真的能看出来，这是一辆半挂卡车
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.86,0:17:22.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,being built by an auto manufacturer.\N由一家汽车制造商建造的。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.06,0:17:27.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just again, the smooth load paths, the crush cans, I've never really seen so much deliberate energy management in a\N再次强调，平滑的载荷路径和溃缩吸能盒，我从未见过如此精心设计的能量管理。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.62,0:17:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,lot of these kind of class eight vehicles that we kind of I looked around very very briefly, just looking through\N这类八级车辆有很多，我刚才匆匆浏览了一下，仅做简单查看。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.54,0:17:34.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, your Freightliners, your Macs,\N你知道的，你们的弗雷特林卡车，你们的麦金塔电脑，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.54,0:17:36.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,your Volvos, and some of those other vehicles.\N你的沃尔沃，还有那些其他车辆。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.47,0:17:40.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They essentially disassociate all structure um from the cab forward of\N它们基本上将驾驶室前方的所有结构都解耦了。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.94,0:17:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,the vehicle cuz realistically, it's it's engine, it's almost like a I don't know the best way to put it,\N这辆车，说实话，它的发动机，几乎就像……我不知道该怎么说才好，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.22,0:17:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,like an immovable object when you really get down to it of how much um space is is taken there, and frankly, what\N说到底，那里的空间占用究竟有多大，其实就像一个不可移动的物体，坦白讲，这很关键。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.18,0:17:59.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,energy, if you were in an impact, is being absorbed there or hits, and how it reacts to the rest of the vehicle.\N如果发生碰撞，能量是在那里被吸收，还是撞击到其他部位，以及车辆其余部分的反应如何。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.62,0:18:00.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I think uh this is Suchi Kesh.\N呃，我想这是苏奇·凯什。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.04,0:18:03.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm the process engineer for the body weight shop.\N我是车身车间的工艺工程师。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.56,0:18:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is body weight area for\N呃，这是体重区域
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.02,0:18:11.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,high roof assembly. Uh so, let me give you some background about high roof and its manufacturing line. So, this\N高顶棚总成。嗯，让我先跟你们介绍一下高顶棚及其生产线的背景。所以，这个
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.86,0:18:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,aerodynamic assembly is manufactured entirely from aluminum material to reduce the overall vehicle weight while\N空气动力学组件完全采用铝材制造，以减轻整车重量，同时
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.26,0:18:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,maintaining its structural strength. Uh it also uh Uh we have the uh joining technologies,\N保持其结构强度。嗯，我们还有连接技术，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.70,0:18:31.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,different joining technologies, such as uh resistance spot welding, clinching process, and also our adhesive\N不同的连接技术，例如电阻点焊、铆接工艺，以及我们的胶粘技术
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.26,0:18:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,application process uh to create this uh whole joint assembly.\N申请流程，用于创建这个完整的联合组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.14,0:18:38.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the stage the production of the high roof is divided into two stages.\N啊，高屋顶的生产分为两个阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.05,0:18:41.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,First one is the high roof bracket line, where\N第一个是高屋顶支架线，
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.34,0:18:43.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,we join all the small brackets on together by using the joining\N我们通过连接将所有小括号合并在一起。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.83,0:18:48.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,technologies and transfer it to the downstream process. And the second stage\N技术并将其传递到下游流程。第二阶段
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.66,0:18:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,is the high roof uh assembly line, where we uh join the side skin, uh top skin,\N是高顶棚的装配线，我们在这里将侧边蒙皮和顶部蒙皮拼接起来。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.42,0:18:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and uh by using those brackets and create the finished whole assembly. At the end of the process, we unload this\N然后用这些夹具，完成整个组件的装配。过程结束后，我们将其卸下。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.98,0:19:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,finished whole assembly on the conveyor and send it to the pre-coat, which is the downstream process for the whole\N完成传送带上的全部装配后，将其送入前涂装工序，这是整体流程的下游环节。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.66,0:19:05.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,body weight shop.\N体重商店。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.08,0:19:12.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone. My name is David Couples. I'm the associate manager for body and white and coatings. Uh as Suchi\N大家好，我是大卫·科平斯，车身与涂料副经理。如须知
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.74,0:19:14.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Kesh said, there's a lot of complex engineering and manufacturing\N凯什说，这里面涉及大量复杂的工程和制造。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.01,0:19:17.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,that goes into the production of one of these high\N这会投入其中一台高端产品的生产中
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.02,0:19:19.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,roofs. We'll walk a little bit more into the benefits the\N屋顶。我们再深入探讨一下其带来的好处。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.75,0:19:24.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Semi gets from having them high roof manufactured this way.\N半体从以这种方式制造的高顶结构中获益。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.06,0:19:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The number that may surprise you is that this high roof only weighs about 170 lb,\N可能让你惊讶的是，这个高屋顶的重量只有约170磅。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.78,0:19:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it has over 700 welds on it. That's a lot of manufacturing that goes into a product that's this light. Not only\N但它上面有超过700个焊点，制造这样一个轻量化产品，需要如此多的工艺流程。不仅如此
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.46,0:19:36.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,that,\N那个，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.34,0:19:38.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,we just don't build the high roof to add another structure to the cabin.\N我们只是没有在舱顶再建一个高屋顶结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.41,0:19:42.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't just build a high roof to make it have that sleek design that makes it look\N我们不只是建一个高屋顶，只为让其拥有流线型设计，看起来更美观。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.02,0:19:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,really cool going down the road. We build the high roof to improve our aerodynamics. So, that said, as the\N真的很酷，一路飞驰。我们加高车顶，以优化空气动力学性能。这么说来，
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.66,0:19:55.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,cabin moves down the highway, and there's a lot of air that pushes up against it, the high roof helps redirect\N车厢在高速公路上行驶时，会有大量空气向上推挤，较高的车顶有助于引导气流。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.82,0:20:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,that air over the trailer. It gives us more range. It gives us a better energy efficiency. That said, that's super\N车顶的空气流过拖车，能增加续航，提升能源效率。不过，这已经非常出色了。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.34,0:20:08.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,important for a class 8 vehicle. This going to spend most of its life riding up and down the freeway at highway\N对8级车辆来说非常重要，它大部分时间都将在高速公路上来回行驶。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.46,0:20:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,speeds. That's a lot of air to move around. And ultimately, we're trying to hit that 1.7 kW per hour\N这需要推动大量空气，最终目标是实现每小时1.7千瓦的能效。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.14,0:20:18.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,per mile to give us that effective range for our long-range vehicles\N每英里的成本，以实现我们长距离车辆的有效续航里程
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.18,0:20:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,of 500 miles for a full charge. That said, every time\N500英里满电续航。不过，每次
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.14,0:20:24.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,we produce one of these, we're not just producing another part.\N我们生产的是其中一台，而不仅仅是在制造另一个零件。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.47,0:20:28.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we're doing is we're producing a functional part of\N我们正在生产一个功能部件。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.18,0:20:35.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,a system that really takes mechanical precision and translates that over to aerodynamic efficiency, energy\N一个真正将机械精度转化为气动效率与能源效率的系统
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.06,0:20:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,efficiency, and ultimately vehicle range.\N效率，最终决定车辆的续航里程。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.34,0:20:42.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Guys, my name is Jay. This is Marco, and this is the coatings line.\N各位，我叫杰伊，这是马可，这是涂层生产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.82,0:20:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tesla's legacy vehicle manufacturing facilities are built around a technology that has\N特斯拉的 legacy 车辆制造工厂是围绕一项技术建立的，这项技术
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.82,0:20:51.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,been the industry standard for decades, liquid paint.\N几十年来一直是行业标准的液态涂料。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.04,0:20:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we designed this uh, sub uh,\N当我们设计这个子……
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.26,0:21:05.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Semi we didn't just design a new truck, we designed a manufacturing\N我们不仅设计了一辆新车，更重新设计了整个制造流程。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.70,0:21:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,process from the ground up.\N从零开始构建。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.74,0:21:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We challenged every coating requirement we have. Corrosion protection, UV stability,\N我们挑战了所有涂层要求，包括防腐蚀和抗紫外线稳定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.74,0:21:20.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,long-term durability, stone chip resistance, and of course, aesthetics.\N长期耐用性、抗石击性，以及当然的美观性。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.38,0:21:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We asked ourselves, does it have to be liquid paint?\N我们问自己，它非得是液体涂料不可吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.94,0:21:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the answer was no.\N答案是否定的。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.74,0:21:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we turned to powder coating, which we actually have a lot of experience with from our energy products.\N于是，我们转向了粉末涂层，这其实是我们能源产品领域中非常有经验的技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.10,0:21:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,But to make powder coating work at this scale,\N但要让粉末涂料在这一规模下发挥作用，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.82,0:21:39.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,we had to make some deliberate engineering decisions from day one,\N从第一天起，我们就必须做出一些明确的工程决策。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.98,0:21:45.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,which meant selecting the right substrate, the correct fastening material and methods.\N这意味着要选择合适的基板、正确的紧固材料和方法。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.80,0:21:53.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we also influenced part geometry.\N我们还影响了零件的几何形状。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.22,0:21:57.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the results are this coatings line you see behind me.\N结果就是我身后的这道涂层生产线。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.82,0:22:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This line is 1/3 the size of a equivalent liquid paint line.\N这条线的尺寸仅为同等液态涂料线的三分之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.42,0:22:07.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has less waste, essentially zero VOCs,\N它产生的废弃物更少，几乎不产生挥发性有机物。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.74,0:22:13.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we think it brings the best value to our customers.\N我们认为这为客户带来了最佳价值。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.42,0:22:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Marco will walk you through the process.\N马科将为您演示整个流程。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.46,0:22:18.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you everyone, and thank you for being here.\N谢谢大家，也谢谢你们的到来。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.54,0:22:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh coating system makes a step on the process, where we give the preparation of surface. We have two main processes\N涂层系统在工艺上迈出了一步，即对表面进行预处理。我们有两个主要工艺。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.70,0:22:30.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,to do that. The first one already Rob mentioned, we have a pre-treatment,\N要做到这一点。第一个，罗布已经提到了，我们有预处理，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.34,0:22:37.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we clean all the surfaces and prepare with the first layer, so we can prepare all the surface to add and get\N我们清洁所有表面并涂上第一层，以便为后续添加做好准备
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.14,0:22:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,bond the paint.\N粘合油漆。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.50,0:22:43.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,After that, we seal it the cabin, so it is prepared for the road.\N之后，我们密封舱体，使其做好上路准备。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.06,0:22:48.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the last part and the main is where we do the magic come from.\N最后一部分也是最关键的部分，正是魔法诞生的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.10,0:22:50.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,We spray the powder color to give every part of\N我们喷上粉末颜色，让每个部分都着色。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.41,0:22:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the body the color that we are uh uh\N身体的颜色，就是我们所说的那种颜色
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.78,0:22:57.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,well, delivering to our clients. So,\N嗯，为客户交付产品。所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.22,0:23:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,these many layers of protection give us all the warranty that we are giving a last longer duration,\N这些层层防护让我们完全有保障，确保产品使用寿命更长。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.58,0:23:09.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,and give us a high durability on our buses. Thank you so much.\N还能大幅提升公交车的耐用性，非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.10,0:23:13.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, the next station, I believe um actually there's roofs prior to this,\N所以，下一站，我认为，呃，实际上在这之前还有屋顶。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.54,0:23:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,but we can kind of speak to that here as well.\N不过我们也可以在这里谈一下这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.70,0:23:17.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So, I'll kind of go into that very, very briefly. So,\N嗯，我就简单快速地讲一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.91,0:23:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,when you look at the truck and it's kind of overall aero feature on\N当你看这辆卡车时，它整体上的空气动力学特性
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.14,0:23:26.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,top, um and cuz it kind of ties in with essentially the other panels that are here. So, generally speaking on the a\N首先，嗯，因为这其实和这里其他小组讨论的内容有些关联。所以总的来说，在AI方面
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.50,0:23:27.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,lot of these vehicles,\N这些车辆中有很多
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.26,0:23:30.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,um your hoods, your fenders, your aero skirts,\N你的引擎盖、挡泥板、空气动力学侧裙，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.52,0:23:36.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,um and everything realistically kind of your big class A surfaces are\N嗯，实际上，你那些大型A级曲面
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.54,0:23:39.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,typically composite. Um there's nothing necessarily wrong with them.\N通常是复合材料。嗯，它们本身并没有什么问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.98,0:23:46.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,They often time are essentially like a slurry of a fiberglass or a rolled mat, something to that that effect.\N它们通常本质上就像玻璃纤维浆料或卷状毡料，类似这样的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.10,0:23:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They often times are relatively heavy, they're large, and um they're expensive.\N它们通常比较重，体积大，而且很贵。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.94,0:23:57.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have some I personally have some very direct experience with dealing with large composite panels, and sometimes\N我有一些直接经验，处理过大型复合面板，有时候
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.02,0:24:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're they're absolute right call, um but I can see exactly why a lot of the\N他们说得完全正确，嗯，但我完全理解为什么很多人会这样想。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.06,0:24:09.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,features and panels that we'd see on more traditional trucks, Tesla brought in-house, stamped them, and then powder\N特斯拉将传统卡车上的各种零部件和面板收归内部，自行冲压成型并进行粉末喷涂。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.62,0:24:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,coated them. So,\N涂上它们。所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.54,0:24:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,um nothing too, too crazy as far as the the roof aero there, since they have large panels,\N至于车顶空气动力学，他们用了大面积的面板，所以没什么特别夸张的设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.14,0:24:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit of buckling that we kind of saw, but realistically,\N出现了一点点屈曲，但我们实际上看到的并不多。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.06,0:24:25.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's built up um much like what you see here as far as internal um like top hat structures supporting it. I\N它的内部结构类似于这里看到的顶帽结构，用来支撑整体。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.38,0:24:29.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,would argue it's probably lighter than your conventional um composite structure, but we'll see,\N我认为它可能比传统的复合结构更轻，但还得看看。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.58,0:24:31.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe we'll tear it down in the future.\N也许将来我们会把它拆掉。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.82,0:24:34.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,But one thing I really kind of wanted to focus on is,\N但有一点我特别想强调的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.76,0:24:39.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's difficult to see, I did talk with someone while we were there,\N而且很难看清，我当时在那里时和一个人聊过。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.50,0:24:41.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,um just briefly, but you can see a little bit of the sheen here.\N呃，简单说一下，但你可以看到这里有一点光泽。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.52,0:24:45.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I don't know for sure, but I we talked about it. They said they're not doing\N我不太确定，但我们聊过，他们说他们不打算做。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.94,0:24:50.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,any liquid traditional coatings here.\N这里的液体传统涂料。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:50.22,0:24:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,They really stressed essentially um challenging all their coating\N他们重点强调了，基本上就是挑战他们所有的涂层。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.06,0:24:59.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,requirements and painting requirements for the cab, and I would believe that cuz it does appear um based off the\N驾驶室的配置要求和涂装要求，我相信这一点，因为确实看起来是基于这个
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.82,0:25:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,sheen and how that kind of transitions upward that they're they're not really,\N她和那种向上的转变，他们其实并不是真的……
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.30,0:25:05.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, kind of doing a traditional e-coat or bath here.\N你知道，就像在这里进行传统的电泳涂装或浸涂一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.74,0:25:10.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I asked and I was told that essentially a lot of these\N呃，我问过，被告知基本上这些
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.22,0:25:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,cavities are raw, which means in the coil process um they have a a relatively slick coating that they're using to\N腔体是未经处理的，这意味着在绕线过程中，它们使用了一种相对光滑的涂层。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.70,0:25:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,prevent corrosion here. Obviously,\N防止此处腐蚀。显然，
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.66,0:25:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,aluminum is is naturally a little bit resistant to that, but you do have to prep its surface for bonding.\N铝本身具有一定的耐腐蚀性，但你仍需对表面进行处理以利于粘接。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.30,0:25:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, that's something that that is I think very noteworthy. Maybe not that big of a deal, but I know um getting\N所以，这是一件我认为非常值得注意的事。也许不算什么大事，但我知道，获得
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.30,0:25:31.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of our customers to do that would be very, very difficult.\N我们的一些客户要实现这一点会非常非常困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.80,0:25:34.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,If that is in fact true, it's hard to tell from this\N如果事实真是如此，仅凭这个很难判断
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.58,0:25:36.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,particular image, but it did uh appear while we were there to\N特定的图像，不过我们在那里时它确实出现了
Dialogue: 0,0:25:36.69,0:25:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,be much more um metallic and uh not like essentially a traditional\N要更金属化一些，而不是像传统的那样
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.18,0:25:47.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,vehicle where you can kind of see here where what is painted off to the side here or the the light we have there\N你可以看到这里侧面涂装的部分，或者这里的灯光位置
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.18,0:25:51.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,clearly a gray e-coat um that's being applied to the body and then the the top coat that's over it.\N显然是一种灰色的电泳涂层，正在喷涂在车身表面，然后是其上的面漆。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.22,0:25:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to hand the mic over to Audrey who's going to show you a demonstration of the motorized seat belt.\N接下来我把话筒交给奥黛丽，她将为大家演示电动安全带。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.18,0:26:02.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, just a quick warning for anyone who is a bit sensitive or easily startled,\N所以，提醒一下，对惊吓比较敏感的人请注意，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.22,0:26:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh the belts are active. Uh the best way to experience this demo is to click the\N啊，皮带正在运行。体验这个演示的最佳方式是点击这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.78,0:26:09.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,belt in, pull out a little slack.\N系好安全带，拉出一点 slack。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.50,0:26:16.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you'll see that the belt will pull it in activate mode. Just like that. And\N你会看到皮带会将其拉入激活模式，就这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.50,0:26:18.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,then you will feel a belt vibration.\N然后你会感觉到腰带震动。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:18.42,0:26:24.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like that. Once you feel that, lean forward and the belt will pull you back into the seat.\N感觉到了吗？身体前倾，安全带就会把你拉回座位。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:24.18,0:26:29.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're building seats completely in house. We saw a little bit of the line where they're kidding up foam. I'm not\N他们正在内部完全自主地制造座椅。我们看到生产线的一小段，他们正在给泡沫材料做处理。我不
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.94,0:26:34.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,sure if they're pouring foam there and actually making seat foam or if essentially this is an internal directed\N反正他们是在灌注泡沫，真的在做座椅泡沫，还是说这本质上就是一种内部定向
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.98,0:26:40.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,design and then a lot of the upper portion of the structure is essentially designed by Tesla, owned by Tesla,\N设计完成后，该结构的上半部分基本上由特斯拉设计并归特斯拉所有。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.22,0:26:43.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,shipped in, and then essentially they're just building it here.\N运抵后，基本上就在这里直接组装了。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.03,0:26:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could see essentially very deliberate material and\N你可以明显看出，这些材料显然是经过精心挑选的。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.54,0:26:49.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,manufacturing strategies. So, the seat base itself is a large casting.\N制造策略。因此，座椅底座本身就是一个大型铸件。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.73,0:26:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you have the integration here with essentially the um\N嗯，这里基本上实现了集成，呃
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.66,0:26:57.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,pneumatic strut essentially adjusting the seat height itself.\N气动支柱实际上可以自动调节座椅高度。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.14,0:27:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Inside of that is actually a very very large um extrusion. It has smaller cavities here\N里面实际上是一个非常大的凸起，这里还有较小的空腔。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.14,0:27:06.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,off to the side to kind of facilitate some mounting points.\N在旁边设置，以便于安装。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.82,0:27:08.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um what's notable about that is, you know,\N值得注意的是，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.34,0:27:13.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,extrusions are relatively inexpensive to get into um and essentially like floor space.\N型材相对容易获取，基本上就像获取地面空间一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:13.83,0:27:14.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,\N所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.25,0:27:20.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,both of these strategies, the floor space that it would take to make them is is significantly less than essentially\N这两种策略所需占用的地面空间，相比而言要少得多
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.82,0:27:26.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh a large or, you know, medium-size stamped assembly um with all the fixturing that's needed. So, when I kind\N嗯，一个大型或中型冲压件装配体，带有所有必要的夹具。所以，当我……
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.58,0:27:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,of look at this in general, if there is a theme that is one of the themes they seem to be balancing is essentially\N总的来说，如果有一个主题，那就是他们似乎在努力平衡的一个核心主题
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.98,0:27:35.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,floor space required for some of their processes.\N部分工艺所需的占地面积。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.38,0:27:37.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,It comes up into essentially a stamped uh steel assembly for\N它最终形成一个近乎冲压成型的钢制组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.06,0:27:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,the hinges and the power elements there. Again, that makes\N铰链和电源元件在那里。再次强调，这使得
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.58,0:27:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,sense to me.\N对我而言有意义。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.58,0:27:44.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I believe this is the seat back itself.\N我相信这就是座椅靠背本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.74,0:27:50.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, steel is ductile. Um there's a lot of loads that go into this, so it makes sense that essentially they\N你知道，钢材具有延展性。这里承受着很大的载荷，所以本质上它们这样设计是合理的。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.50,0:27:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,leverage steel here um for its properties and it's it's well-suited to perform there as well. So, in general,\N这里利用钢材的特性，它同样非常适合承担这一任务。总的来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.74,0:27:59.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not as actually sure how much is being done and manufactured uh on-site,\N我其实不太确定现场有多少是真正被完成和制造的。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.45,0:28:03.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it is being assembled uh completely on-site there cuz the line is\N但它是在现场完全组装的，因为生产线就在那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.02,0:28:07.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,just behind here where all these seats are being kitted up and built.\N就在这儿，所有座椅正在被装配和安装。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.66,0:28:14.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I'm Oliver and this is Chris and we're both on the axle production engineering team. Uh so, these are the\N我是奥利弗，这是克里斯，我们俩都在轴生产工程团队。所以，这些是
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.66,0:28:21.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,four products that we build um in the axle part of the factory. Uh first in the middle there on the table,\N我们在工厂的轴部件部分开发了四款产品。首先，中间桌上的那款，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.30,0:28:25.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's our permanent magnet motor. Uh so, that's kind of the heart of the gearbox.\N这就是我们的永磁电机，可以说是变速箱的核心所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.21,0:28:30.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh that's how we actually generate power. So, the cool thing about\N这就是我们实际发电的方式。所以有趣的是
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.06,0:28:35.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,this axle is that each of the motors are independent of each other and they both\N这根轴的特点是，每个电机彼此独立，两者都是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.82,0:28:39.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,control uh each hub and each side of the wheels independent of each other.\N控制每个轮毂和每个车轮都能独立运作。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.76,0:28:47.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so because of the structural similarities between the efficiency axle and the torque axle, these are actually\N是的，由于效率轴和扭矩轴之间存在结构相似性，这两个轴实际上
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.86,0:28:49.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,assembled on the same exact line.\N在同一根线上组装。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:49.50,0:28:54.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so they share the same line, but they also share a couple of the same parts like the heat exchanger, uh the oil\N嗯，它们共用同一条生产线，还共用了一些相同的部件，比如散热器、油路系统等。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.98,0:28:56.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,pump, and the oil filter.\N油泵和机油滤清器。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.94,0:28:59.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then various bolts with other other other Tesla vehicles.\N还有各种与其他特斯拉车型共用的螺栓。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.38,0:29:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the stator and the drive inverter are actually also used in the Cybertruck.\N实际上，定子和驱动逆变器也用在 Cybertruck 上。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.74,0:29:11.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so toward the end of our assembly line, we also do a calibration to make sure that we are sending out something\N因此，在我们装配线的最后阶段，我们还会进行一次校准，以确保我们发出的产品是准确无误的。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.70,0:29:18.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the peak motor efficiency uh and peak power output. Once we calibrate the motor, it moves into the dyno test\N在达到峰值电机效率和峰值功率输出后，电机校准完毕，便进入测功机测试。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.66,0:29:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,station where we uh attach large absorber motors to measure the uh mechanical power out of the motors\N我们在这里将大型吸收电机安装到位，以测量电机输出的机械功率。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:24.14,0:29:26.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,independently.\N独立地。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.74,0:29:33.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,While we're doing that, we also have uh vibration sensors that are touching on once the gearbox to um\N与此同时，我们还安装了振动传感器，直接接触变速箱以进行监测。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.82,0:29:41.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,detect for any uh knocks or like vibrations that might cause any noise to the customer um or indicate early life\N检测是否有敲击声或类似振动，这些可能会引起客户噪音，或表明早期寿命问题
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.10,0:29:43.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,failure of the bearings of the gears.\N齿轮轴承的失效。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.14,0:29:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So after testing's done, we add some of the chassis components, and then we pack it onto the cart that you see here\N测试完成后，我们安装部分机箱组件，然后将其装到眼前的推车上
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.10,0:29:54.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh which is then automated automatically delivered across the hallway through this bay door directly consumed by\N然后通过这个侧门自动传送至走廊另一侧，直接被使用
Dialogue: 0,0:29:54.82,0:29:55.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,general assembly.\N全体大会
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.78,0:30:03.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um So last, we have our steer axle. It's kind of in the back. Uh so what's unique about the steer axle\N嗯，最后是我们的转向轴，它在后面一点。嗯，这个转向轴有什么特别之处呢
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.62,0:30:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,is that it has an independent front suspension,\N因为它配备了独立前悬架，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.02,0:30:11.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,which allows for us to have a really tight wheel cut and in turn has\N这使我们能够实现非常紧凑的转向，从而提升操控性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.70,0:30:14.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,a really tight uh turn radius. So if you guys have already done your drive-thrus,\N一个非常紧凑的转弯半径。所以你们如果已经开过自助车道了，
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.14,0:30:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,you might have it's kind of remarkable how how tight it is.\N你可能觉得，它竟然这么紧凑，真是有点惊人。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:17.98,0:30:22.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's actually comparable to a Model Y how tight it is.\N实际上，它的空间紧凑程度和 Model Y 差不多。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.66,0:30:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,My favorite part of the vehicle we got to see essentially the front um the front cradle.\N我最喜欢的部分是车体前部，也就是前部车架。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.42,0:30:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Super high level,\N极高层级
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.26,0:30:35.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,very large cast iron castings for each side essentially integrated um shock tower, upper control arm mounting\N每侧的大型铸铁件基本上是集成的，包括减震塔和上控制臂安装座。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.66,0:30:39.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,point, and then essentially there's provisions that reach down to these stanchions here.\N然后，有一些支撑结构延伸到这里的立柱上。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.54,0:30:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um these are unique for each side. These aluminum stanchions shoot down here.\N这些支架每侧都有其独特设计，铝制支架向下延伸。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:45.82,0:30:46.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,They pick up on a large aluminum casting the center.\N他们拿起中间的一个大型铝铸件。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.90,0:30:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's very difficult to see actually a little bit bigger here on a\N实际上很难看清，这里稍微大一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.66,0:30:52.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,huge screen.\N巨大的屏幕。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.90,0:30:54.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but the steering rack is here. It's based off the Cybertruck\N但转向机架在这里，它是基于 Cybertruck 设计的。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.36,0:30:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,mostly from the perspective of of the board and some of\N主要从董事会的角度，以及部分
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.58,0:31:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,the controlling electronics, but realistically when you look at it, it was difficult to see here or even on the\N控制电子元件，但实际情况是，从这里看，甚至在屏幕上都很难看清。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.26,0:31:10.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,line a little bit later. It looks nothing like um the Cybertruck. So they're leveraging\N稍晚一点再上线。看起来完全不像那个 Cybertruck。所以他们正在利用
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.06,0:31:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially um the controls and the boards. They're high-cost um items and borrowing that from the Cybertruck get\N本质上，这些控制模块和电路板都是高成本的部件，从 Cybertruck 上借鉴过来的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.46,0:31:18.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,get getting good good good prices and um and leveraging,\N拿到好价格，还有利用……
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.23,0:31:22.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, the their vertical integration. But realistically\N你知道，他们的垂直整合。但现实来说
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.42,0:31:24.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,everything else seems to be tailored for the Tesla Semi.\N其他一切似乎都是为特斯拉半挂卡车量身定制的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.13,0:31:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we kind of looking at this more specifically when it's on\N当我们更具体地来看它在运行时的情况
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.98,0:31:30.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,the vehicle, you know, to me the aluminum outriggers were mostly for crash.\N这辆车，你知道的，对我来说，铝合金支架主要是为了防撞。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.73,0:31:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then I kind of was wondering about size. Um so when we got a little\N然后我开始好奇起尺寸来。嗯，当我们拿到一点的时候
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.50,0:31:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,bit farther through the tour, I'd asked a a counterpart from Tesla there what was the driving um you know, force\N参观再深入一点，我曾问过特斯拉那边的一位同行，驱动他们前进的真正动力是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.58,0:31:48.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,behind essentially the disassociated cradle and the aluminum stanchions and he said\N本质上是脱离了支架和铝制立柱，他说
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.38,0:31:54.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,packaging. And more specifically um rack density with shipping. And that makes complete sense to me, right? I\N封装，更具体地说是运输过程中的机架密度，这完全说得通，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.86,0:32:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,mean this is a very very large piece. By splitting this, breaking this up, you can shrink this, get this inside and\N意思是这是一块非常非常大的部件。通过拆分它、把它分解，你可以缩小它的尺寸，让它得以装入内部。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.14,0:32:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,probably ship double the amount of if not, you know, triple the amount of shock towers um to the facility there in\N可能要运两倍，甚至三倍的冲击塔到那个设施去
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.26,0:32:13.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sparks. And then, you know, managing some of the energy um was secondary as far as having these\N火花。然后，你知道，管理部分能量，对于拥有这些来说是次要的。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.90,0:32:16.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,be aluminum extrusions reaching down to this casting itself.\N是延伸至铸件本身的铝挤压件。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.25,0:32:20.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can really see here from essentially the knuckle\N你几乎可以从指节处清楚地看到
Dialogue: 0,0:32:20.34,0:32:22.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,outward, there's kind of a lot of more commodity-based items as far\N向外看，有很多更偏向于商品化的物品。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.41,0:32:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,as um the air brakes and such nature that keep the\N就像空气制动器之类的东西，能自然地保持稳定
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.50,0:32:29.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,vehicle up and running while it's operating.\N车辆在运行时保持启动状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.62,0:32:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a lot of the stuff here is more traditional, but essentially when you get essentially from that unit bearing,\N这里的很多东西都比较传统，但本质上，当你从那个轴承单元开始时，
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.86,0:32:41.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will, inboard, that's where really the uniqueness of the Tesla starts to kind of come into its own. Um\N如果你愿意的话，内部安装才是特斯拉真正独特之处开始凸显的地方。嗯
Dialogue: 0,0:32:41.38,0:32:44.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,in contrast to essentially kind of your your hubs and the the brakes,\N与你所谓的枢纽和刹车本质上完全不同，
Dialogue: 0,0:32:44.21,0:32:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's a lot of commodity-based items leveraging\N这些是大量基于商品的项目，正在利用……
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.66,0:32:49.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,again what the the industry has already um uh out there and\N再说一遍，业界已经有的那些东西
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.45,0:32:53.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,what they can do to get a good cost. More specifically, just\N他们能做什么来获得良好的成本。更具体地说，仅仅
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.42,0:32:56.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,keep the trucks running. You know, that was one of the themes in\N让卡车持续运行。你知道，这正是其中一个主题。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.44,0:33:00.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,general that we heard is um high up times. And early in\N我们听到的普遍反馈是，时间非常紧张。而且刚开始就……
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.14,0:33:01.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,development when they were doing this,\N他们在进行这项开发时
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.66,0:33:05.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,yeah, they had some things break down and things of that nature, but towards the end, especially from the test\N是的，他们有些东西出了故障，类似的情况，但到了最后，尤其是测试阶段
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.62,0:33:06.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,drivers that we were talking to, he was like,\N我们之前聊到的那些司机，他当时说，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.04,0:33:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,"They just don't really break down anymore." And if there is an issue,\N它们现在基本上不再出问题了。如果有问题的话，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.02,0:33:15.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,they're typically back on the road in like 30 or 40 minutes. And uh I think when you look at their their overall\N通常30到40分钟内就能重新上路。而且我认为，从整体来看
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.46,0:33:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,manufacturing strategy, you can see um that aspect of prioritizing the commodities where it makes sense, and\N制造策略方面，你可以看到，优先考虑那些有意义的原材料，这一点显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.90,0:33:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,then tailoring things to get good prices and good function um where it needs to be. So, the drive axles, we spoke a\N然后根据需求调整配置，以获得良好的价格和性能。比如驱动轴，我们之前提到过。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.10,0:33:29.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,little bit about this earlier. Um I kind of threw an image\N关于这个，之前提过一点。呃，我大概扔了一张图
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.08,0:33:33.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,here of the actual um the rotor here um that was developed\N这里实际的旋翼，就是这个，是研发出来的
Dialogue: 0,0:33:33.06,0:33:34.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,specifically for this. It is based off the Cybertruck.\N具体来说，它是基于 Cybertruck 的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.64,0:33:38.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They tweaked some things to get the volume where they wanted to,\N他们调整了一些参数，把音量调到了想要的程度。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.22,0:33:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,and more specifically, you know, magnet alignment to get the performance where they wanted.\N更具体地说，就是磁体对齐，以达到他们想要的性能。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.58,0:33:48.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very different as far as its overall like architectural setup as far as the orientation of the drive module, where\N在整体架构布局以及驱动模块的朝向方面，差异非常大。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.14,0:33:55.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the inverter is in comparison to some other things we've seen in the e-beam space, especially especially in the\N与我们在电子束领域见过的其他一些技术相比，这个逆变器显得尤为突出，尤其是特别突出。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.06,0:33:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Class 8s um kind of segment itself.\N8级车本身就是一个类别。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.78,0:33:59.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone kept comparing like the size of the rotor um to just other things,\N大家总是在拿螺旋桨的尺寸和其他东西比较。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.47,0:34:01.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,what water bottles, whatever they had on\N什么水瓶，他们有的都行
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.82,0:34:08.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,hand, picking them up, looking at their hands, and just making the comment of the size difference in comparing this\N用手拿起它们，看着自己的手，然后只是评论了一下两者在尺寸上的差异
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.22,0:34:10.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially to uh one of the six cylinders or so that\N基本上是六个气缸中的一个左右
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.17,0:34:14.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,would power a traditional diesel truck, and just how much smaller\N足以驱动一辆传统柴油卡车，而且体积小得多
Dialogue: 0,0:34:14.82,0:34:19.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will, the power is kind of contained within um the Tesla Semi.\N如果你愿意的话，特斯拉半挂卡车的电力基本上是被封闭在内部的。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.66,0:34:24.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, you're kind of robbing Peter to pay Paul as far as where the complexity and the the weight is.\N显然，从复杂性和重量的分配来看，你这有点儿是拆东墙补西墙。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:24.18,0:34:27.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but it's undeniable when you look at how much compact how\N但不可否认的是，当你看到它的紧凑程度时，
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.84,0:34:32.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,much more compact the powertrain is in relation to the the\N动力系统相比而言要紧凑得多
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.34,0:34:33.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,e-beam in a versus a conventional truck.\N电子束与传统卡车的对比。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.90,0:34:37.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone. I hope you guys are having a great day so far.\N大家好，希望你们今天过得愉快。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.46,0:34:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,My name is Adon Berwa and I am the process engineer for this line known as the automated battery marriage line.\N我叫阿东·伯瓦，是这条名为自动电池配对线的产线工艺工程师。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.18,0:34:49.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone. I'm Darshan. I'm the quality engineer for the battery marriage line that you're seeing right now.\N大家好，我是达尚，目前负责你们正在观看的电池嫁接生产线的质量工程工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:49.32,0:34:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So as you can see in front of you and as the name suggests this is a completely automated line. I\N正如你们眼前所见，正如其名称所示，这是一条完全自动化的生产线。我
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.38,0:35:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,believe the only manual thing on this line is the bulk loading which is done by an operator. However,\N这条线上唯一需要人工操作的只有批量装载，由操作员完成。不过
Dialogue: 0,0:35:03.82,0:35:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,the sub packs or the battery packs are delivered to us on automated mobile robots. They enter the cell over here.\N电池包由自动移动机器人运送至我们这里，它们从这里进入工位。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.42,0:35:13.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once the robot is in position the auto loader will actually pick\N机器人就位后，自动装载机将开始执行抓取
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.69,0:35:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,up the battery pack from the robot and place it onto\N从机器人上取下电池组，然后放上去
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.90,0:35:19.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,one of these pallets. This process will repeat for a total of\N其中一个托盘。这一过程将重复进行，总共达到
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.68,0:35:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,three times for long range, for a total of two times for\N远距离三次，总共两次
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.38,0:35:25.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,standard range.\N标准续航里程。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.02,0:35:29.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once a pallet is fully loaded it is then conveyed automatically\N一旦托盘装满，就会自动传送。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.22,0:35:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,to this loader over or lifter that you see over\N看到的这个吊装设备，或是提升机
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.58,0:35:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,here which lifts the pallet up onto this platform. It then gets positioned\N这里将托盘抬起并放到这个平台上，然后进行定位。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.30,0:35:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,underneath the frame and the carrier actually lowers it down onto the battery\N框架和托架下方实际上会将其降低到电池上。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.70,0:35:48.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,packs. Once that is done, once everything is in position this little\N装好后，一旦所有部件就位，这个小家伙就完成了。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.09,0:35:52.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,shuttle down here with 14 spindles that you see moving right now\N这里有一台穿梭机，配有14个纺锭，你们现在看到它们正在移动。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.98,0:35:55.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually torques all of the battery packs down at once.\N实际上，瞬间对所有电池组施加了扭矩。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.27,0:36:00.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So basically it goes from the the front of the vehicle, torques down\N基本上，它从车辆前部开始，向下施加扭矩
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.02,0:36:02.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,14 bolts, goes to the next pack and next pack and so on.\N14个螺栓，接着装到下一个电池包，再下一个，以此类推。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.96,0:36:07.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,We do all 14 at the same time just to get an even clamp load\N我们同时完成全部14项，以确保夹紧力均匀
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.66,0:36:10.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,across all the bolts.\N所有螺栓上。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:10.10,0:36:15.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Once that's complete the carrier lifts off and then goes down the line for subsequent operations.\N完成之后，运载器起飞，然后沿生产线进行后续操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.86,0:36:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like this is there's a lot going on here in this image.\N这幅图里有很多内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.22,0:36:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very briefly earlier Jordan saw it and he's like man it kind of looks like a like a train. I'm like yeah literally\N刚才乔丹看了一眼，说这玩意儿看起来有点像火车。我说，没错，就是像。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.74,0:36:31.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,looks like a an HO scale train just scaled and magnified up. So here we see the batteries decked on the chassis\N看起来就像一个 HO 比例的火车被放大了。这里我们看到电池组安装在车架上。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.58,0:36:32.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,itself. Um we could probably talk for 2 hours about just\N本身。嗯，我们光是聊这个话题就能聊两个小时。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.35,0:36:36.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,this image going from essentially, you know, the tip of the\N这张图从本质上来说，就像是从尖端开始
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.70,0:36:37.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,vehicle all the way to the the end of it.\N一路开到尽头。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.63,0:36:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we'll hit the high levels kind of going through here. It's impressive to\N嗯，我们会逐步深入到高层内容。这确实令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.70,0:36:43.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,see, uh especially there on the line.\N你看，尤其是那条线上。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.82,0:36:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is about to get on essentially their overhead monorails, which are um I do have a I think another image behind\N这马上就要上到他们的高架单轨系统了，呃，我确实有另一张图片在背后
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.98,0:36:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,it. Kind of looks like the uh the Recognizer from Tron. But, when you look at this, again, like from the beginning,\N有点像《创：战纪》里的识别器。但你看这个，再从头开始看一遍，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.02,0:37:02.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,large castings there uh that are flanking essentially the cradle and the the frame rails on either side. Large uh\N大型铸件位于支架两侧，实际上起到了支撑作用，与两侧的框架梁相呼应。大型的……
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.74,0:37:05.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um extruded aluminum crush cans that then go to an impact structure,\N一个挤压成型的铝制吸能罐，随后进入撞击结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:05.10,0:37:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,which we didn't get a chance to see, but we did\N我们没能看到，但确实看到了
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.86,0:37:10.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,see a little bit about um the substructure behind the front fascia.\N看看前保险杠背后的底座结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.97,0:37:15.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,That in of itself is is interesting. They're doing an in-mold\N这本身就很有趣，他们正在做模内成型。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:15.66,0:37:17.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,film and then shooting behind it. Uh lots of expanded\N拍摄电影，然后在它后面进行拍摄。嗯，大量扩展
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.13,0:37:21.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,polypropylene behind it and then essentially a an in-fascia AGS\N其后是聚丙烯，然后是嵌入式A GS
Dialogue: 0,0:37:21.34,0:37:28.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,system. But, it looks like a car. It doesn't look like anything we've seen on a um on a Semi truck before. Um\N系统。但看起来像辆车，不像我们以前在半挂车上见过的任何东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.94,0:37:32.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,it looks like there is a lot of essentially layering of materials,\N看起来实际上有很多材料的层层叠加，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.06,0:37:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,especially for like low-speed impacts or anything like that.\N尤其是低速碰撞之类的情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.62,0:37:36.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not that it would help you a ton if you were to be hit by\N即使你被击中，这也不会对你有多大帮助
Dialogue: 0,0:37:36.82,0:37:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,something like this. Um but, it does seem like they've learned a lot\N类似这样的东西。嗯，但看起来他们确实学到了很多。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.30,0:37:43.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,for those low-speed impacts because of how critical arrow is for it. Um\N因为箭头在这些低速碰撞中至关重要，所以如此。嗯
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.82,0:37:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually very briefly talking with Lars,\N实际上刚跟拉尔斯简单聊了聊
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.70,0:37:47.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,they split up the whole front fascia into multiple pieces in\N他们把整个前保险杠分成了多个部分
Dialogue: 0,0:37:47.38,0:37:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,part just for this because earlier trucks, they'd break something,\N只是因为之前卡车经常会弄坏东西，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.30,0:37:56.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,they'd hit something, and then essentially start to suffer a little bit of range um performance. And what's this\N它们撞到了东西，然后性能就稍微下降了一点。这是怎么回事
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.62,0:37:57.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,way like the cost aspect of it. So,\N就像它的成本方面一样。所以，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.12,0:38:00.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,they really kind of they took this piece and where they had a\N他们真的把这一部分拿过来，做了调整。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.72,0:38:01.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of an elegant\N一种优雅的感觉
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.78,0:38:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,execution early on,\N早期执行
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.02,0:38:06.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,they added some complexity and the ability to essentially repair this thing and\N他们增加了一些复杂性，以及实际上修复此物的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.12,0:38:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,get the front fascia back up and more specifically maintain that low\N把前保险杠装回去，并且更具体地说，保持低姿态
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.86,0:38:11.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,frontal area to keep the efficiency of the truck high.\N前部面积以保持卡车的效率。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.93,0:38:16.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and they kind of did that when they were essentially bringing\N嗯，他们实际上在引入时就做了类似的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.42,0:38:21.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,the design theme more current um with the newer Teslas given how long this has been in development. But,\N这款设计主题更贴近当下，考虑到新款特斯拉的开发周期较长。但，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.54,0:38:23.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,so, you kind of have those energy impact absorbers coming\N所以，你实际上有那些能量冲击吸收器在起作用
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.59,0:38:26.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,into these large cast iron castings here. They're bolted I\N这些大型铸铁铸件。它们是用螺栓固定的。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.78,0:38:29.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,forgive me, I can't remember, but essentially it's a a spin-on rivet.\N抱歉，我不太记得了，但本质上就是一种旋入式铆钉。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:29.73,0:38:34.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,They use this all throughout um the assembly. They do some traditional\N他们在整个装配过程中都用到了这个，做了一些传统操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.22,0:38:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,large bolts as well.\N还有大螺栓。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:35.74,0:38:36.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,When we were looking at the suspension,\N当我们研究悬挂系统时，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.70,0:38:41.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't know for sure and I've got a better picture of this um that we'll probably put in a different deck, but um\N我不太确定，不过我对这个问题有了更清晰的认识，这部分内容我们可能放到另一套演示文稿里。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.74,0:38:43.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,it looks like upper control arms,\N看起来像上控制臂，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.38,0:38:46.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,knuckles, and lower control arms non-handed, which is awesome. So,\N关节和下控制臂都是非对称的，这太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.11,0:38:51.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're talking about a pair of tools, double the volume for these components.\N你提到的是两套工具，这些组件的体积翻倍了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.22,0:38:52.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,And essentially, when they come in, they just get sequenced.\N本质上，它们进来后，就直接被排序了。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.67,0:38:55.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to go to left-hand side or right-hand side.\N他们会向左或向右移动。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.30,0:38:58.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then they're doing a There's like a a bolt-on interface um for the\N然后他们正在做一个类似可附加的接口，嗯，就是个外接接口。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.36,0:39:02.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,knuckles where they kind of put a handed steering arm on. They bolt that\N关节处他们装上了带手柄的转向臂，然后用螺栓固定。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.90,0:39:05.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,onto it, and that's how they're managing essentially um the unique handed\N然后就这样，他们基本上是通过这种方式来管理独特的手性问题的。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.45,0:39:09.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,provisions for the steering as a separate component. But everything else\N转向系统的独立组件配置。但其他一切
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.66,0:39:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,looks like it is um non-handed. It almost looks like they could have done the same with the uh the\N看起来好像是无手的。它们几乎可以像那样处理……
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.46,0:39:19.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,shock towers themselves, but something drove them to make them unique.\N但真正让它们与众不同的是某种驱动因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.59,0:39:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you look at them, there's some different\N当你看它们时，会发现一些不同
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.14,0:39:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,geometry that shows that it is handed.\N显示其具有手性特征的几何结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.94,0:39:29.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,But essentially, you've got this long roll-formed upper frame that runs all the way to the back, very typical of\N但本质上，你有一个长条形滚压成型的上部框架，一直延伸到后部，这在同类产品中非常典型。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:29.38,0:39:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,what we'd see in these trucks. Um the cradle here is decked\N我们在这辆卡车里看到的。嗯，这里的支架已经装好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.10,0:39:35.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,bolted to the side of the frame, excuse me, riveted. There\N固定在车架侧面，抱歉，是铆接的。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.22,0:39:36.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,are some bolt-on features underneath. I don't know if I have a\N有些附加功能藏在下面。我不知道我有没有
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.78,0:39:40.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,better picture of it, but we'll talk a little bit more of\N更清晰地了解它，但我们会再深入讨论一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.38,0:39:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,that in the future that ties essentially those um bulkhead mounting points that we\N未来这些舱壁安装点将基本连接在一起
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.90,0:39:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,referred to earlier um to from the battery pack to the um the frame itself.\N之前提到的，从电池包到车架本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.54,0:39:56.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then you have the batteries all being brought up to the frame and these uh cast outriggers here.\N然后你看到所有电池都被运送到框架上，还有这里的铸造成型的外伸支架。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.34,0:40:01.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have very large, you know, uh structure here. It's piggybacking off of essentially, you know, battery coolant,\N这里结构非常庞大，实际上是在电池冷却液的基础上叠加的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.70,0:40:04.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,high-voltage wiring. And then essentially, when you look at the protection here,\N高压布线。然后本质上，当你看这里的保护措施时，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.76,0:40:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's got a kind of an interesting material\N它用了一种相当有趣的材料
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.18,0:40:09.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh protection scheme for the side of the packs, but a very,\N啊，这是针对电池包侧面的保护方案，但非常……
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.40,0:40:12.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,very large multi-cell extrusion here. I don't know if it's if\N这里是一个非常大的多腔体挤压。我不确定是不是
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.02,0:40:15.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's e-coat, if it's powder coated. It was difficult to see, and again,\N是电泳漆，如果是粉末喷涂的话。很难看清楚，再次强调，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.40,0:40:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,we were kind of moving through this area pretty\N我们当时正大致穿过这一区域。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:17.90,0:40:22.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,quickly. Um then that goes into essentially a steel assembly above it.\N然后迅速进入其上方的一个钢制组件中。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.46,0:40:26.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that was like a clamshell stamping that's protecting the side of the battery.\N嗯，那就像一个贝壳状的冲压件，用来保护电池的侧面。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.10,0:40:29.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we'll talk more about this in the future, but you know, when you look at essentially where the power electronics\N嗯，我们以后再详细讨论这个问题，但你想想，从本质上来看，功率电子领域
Dialogue: 0,0:40:29.98,0:40:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,were on the side, you know, you have these uber bus bars that are essentially running from where the Megacharger\N你们看，那些超大母排，基本上是从超充桩那里一路延伸过来的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.86,0:40:40.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,interfaces all the way forward. That's all like built offline. This big sub-assembly brought to it. Um you know,\N所有接口都向前延伸，全部都是离线构建的。这个大型子组件被运了过来。嗯，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.46,0:40:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tesla not pioneered, but they really have to leverage essentially large aluminum bus bars for charging. Um and\N特斯拉虽非首创，但他们确实必须利用大型铝制母排来实现充电。嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.82,0:40:48.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's kind of interesting to see how they executed it there.\N有趣的是，看看他们在那里是怎么执行的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.26,0:40:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and then essentially you can see just what they're doing for the protection\N然后你基本上就能看出他们为保护所做的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.18,0:40:55.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,scheme for the side of the vehicle. And then this kind of\N车辆一侧的方案。然后这种
Dialogue: 0,0:40:55.37,0:40:59.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,also supports some of the sub-structure I think in the back\N还支持后部的一些子结构，我想是这样
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.58,0:41:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,and for the cab as well. But overall like it's there's so much here to talk about to kind of unpack. You can see a\N还有驾驶室也是如此。但总的来说，这里有很多内容值得探讨和剖析。你可以看到
Dialogue: 0,0:41:04.78,0:41:10.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,little bit here of the front cooling lines. We'll talk a little bit about the cooling module before we kind of move\N前面一点的冷却管线。我们稍后再谈一下冷却模块。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.62,0:41:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,on. But um you know, in general if I had to say something like thematically a lot of integration, but also a lot of\N嗯，不过总的来说，如果非要说的话，主题上有很多整合，但也有很多……
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.02,0:41:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,serviceability.\N可服务性。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.62,0:41:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you guys have seen the skateboard assembly process.\N你们已经看过滑板的组装过程了。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.82,0:41:30.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh this is our final line cab marriage station. And this whole area is for final line.\N啊，这是我们的最终线缆婚姻站。整个区域都用于最终线缆工序。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.22,0:41:37.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,After the skateboard has finished its quality inspection stations, it comes over to our left and gets dropped onto\N滑板完成质量检测站后，会移到我们左侧，然后被放下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:37.50,0:41:38.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,two automated guided vehicles.\N两辆自动导引车。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.50,0:41:42.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and depending on the variant, long range or standard range,\N嗯，具体取决于型号，长续航版或标准续航版。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.35,0:41:46.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,the AGVs will space themselves accordingly to associate\NAGV 将自动调整间距以实现关联
Dialogue: 0,0:41:46.66,0:41:53.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that. On our left following that, we have our fifth wheel installation station\N在我们左侧，沿着这条路线，是第五轮安装工位。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.06,0:41:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,where the associates will put it in and fasten it.\N由助理们将其放好并固定好。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.18,0:42:03.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then as you see here right now behind me, we have the cab marriage station. This is the world's first fully\N然后你们看到我身后现在这个，就是驾驶室对接站，这是全球首个完全集成的
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.62,0:42:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,automatic cab marriage station.\N自动出租车停靠站。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:05.50,0:42:10.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it requires millimeter level precision to get it to seat accordingly.\N嗯，要让它正确就位，需要毫米级的精度。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.98,0:42:19.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh behind me even more, we have a customer assembly station\N在我身后还有更多，是一个客户组装站
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.42,0:42:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,where every customer's uh cabin is built to their design spec with their custom order.\N每位客户的舱室都根据其设计规格和定制订单量身打造。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.30,0:42:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right? And then we made those to the respective uh skateboard over here.\N对吧？然后我们把这些分别装到了这边的滑板上。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:29.46,0:42:31.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as we kind of move through, we got to see the cooling module. So,\N所以，当我们继续推进时，就能看到冷却模块了。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:31.32,0:42:33.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is something that Dan talked about earlier\N这正是丹 earlier 提到过的事情
Dialogue: 0,0:42:33.70,0:42:36.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the day.\N白天。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.10,0:42:41.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,This was developed um you know, jointly with the cyber cab.\N这是与网络出租车公司联合开发的。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.14,0:42:43.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Much like essentially um you know, the heat pump systems that we have\N就像我们现有的热泵系统一样
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.32,0:42:47.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,seen in the other Teslas and the integration with the octovalve, exactly\N在其他特斯拉车型上也能看到，以及与八通阀的集成，完全一致
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.02,0:42:51.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,what I expected to see when we came here, right? A ton of integration,\N我来这儿时预期看到的，对吧？大量的整合。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.34,0:42:54.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,leveraging the volume of these pumps with what they already build.\N利用这些泵的规模，结合他们现有的生产能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.24,0:42:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'd actually love to see one of these in a uh cyber cab as well cuz\N我倒是很想看看这种车出现在网络出租车里会是什么样子。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:58.90,0:43:00.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's nothing wrong with any of this,\N这些都没有问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:00.22,0:43:04.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you look essentially for the the manifold setup, it's probably about five or six layers, probably hot plated\N但你本质上是在寻找那种流形结构的设置，大概有五到六层，可能是热板的
Dialogue: 0,0:43:04.98,0:43:06.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,together, and just looking at the wiring routing,\N一起看看线路布局，
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.69,0:43:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was wondering how different the the the routing was uh between the\N我在想，这路由之间的差异到底有多大呢。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:11.18,0:43:17.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,two vehicles and if whether you could get essentially some PIA clip features or harness features\N两辆车，如果你能获取一些PIA剪辑功能或运行框架功能
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.62,0:43:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,um in this uh to kind of get some of the clips and some of these other things out, but it may not really make sense\N嗯，为了把一些片段和其他内容先整理出来，但可能听起来并不太通顺。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.10,0:43:27.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,when you're you're packaging into very different environments. So, I think realistically it's normal.\N当你将其打包到各种不同的环境中时，所以我认为从现实角度看，这很正常。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.22,0:43:31.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very efficient cooling systems, it's probably an area where Tesla\N非常高效的冷却系统，这可能是特斯拉的一个优势领域
Dialogue: 0,0:43:31.20,0:43:34.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,spends some of the most effort is getting efficiency\N最费力的环节之一就是提升效率
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.38,0:43:36.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,within these systems. And then essentially you see certain things tailored\N在这些系统中，你基本上会看到某些东西被专门定制。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.72,0:43:40.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,to essentially the environment or specifically the vehicle it is. As\N本质上是环境，或具体来说是车辆本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.22,0:43:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,you see these lines, they're all labeled with tape, they kind of come up here,\N你看这些线，全都用胶带标了号，它们大致从这里往上走。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.46,0:43:47.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then they're um they're set up for the interface to the vehicle.\N然后它们就被设置好，用于与车辆的接口。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:47.38,0:43:50.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And um this cooling module then would be decked in here inside the frame rails,\N然后这个冷却模块就会安装在框架导轨内部。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:50.74,0:43:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you can see all the pipes here. These are\N你可以看到这里的所有管道。这些是
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.74,0:44:01.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,labeled, they correspond with these pipes here as well for the rest of the\N标记后，它们也对应此处的这些管道，其余部分也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.62,0:44:02.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,system for um you know,\N用于你的系统，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:44:02.04,0:44:03.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,the cabin and um battery, you know,\N舱内和电池，你知道的
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.81,0:44:06.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,thermal management.\N热管理
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.38,0:44:08.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,One thing we we didn't really get to see or at least at least we\N有一件事我们其实没怎么看到，至少我们
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.46,0:44:12.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,didn't get an image of. But, um when you look at this, where this would\N没得到图像。但呃，当你看这个时，这会出现在哪里
Dialogue: 0,0:44:12.58,0:44:18.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially sit, you can see it's nested in here. One thing I took from essentially looking at, um both the body\N本质上就是坐着，你可以看到它嵌在这里。我从观察身体结构中得到的一个体会是，嗯，无论是从哪个角度看
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.46,0:44:26.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,in white and wondered based off our Model Y, which has a composite dash, is whether or not we'd see a a little bit\N白色内饰，基于我们的 Model Y，它采用复合材料仪表盘，我想知道我们会不会看到一点变化
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.18,0:44:29.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,more integration between IP, HVAC, and everything there. Um realistically,\NIP、暖通空调以及所有相关系统之间的集成将更加紧密。实际上，
Dialogue: 0,0:44:29.25,0:44:32.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,this uh the dash panel of the Cybersemi looks\N这个 Cybersemi 的仪表盘看起来
Dialogue: 0,0:44:32.94,0:44:34.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,very similar to the Cybertruck. Large pass-throughs both the\N与 Cybertruck 非常相似，前后都设有大型贯通口。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:34.35,0:44:37.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,steering column and a sensor actually their modules that\N转向柱和传感器实际上是它们的模块
Dialogue: 0,0:44:37.34,0:44:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,are mounting there that are part of their essentially overall low-voltage harness system.\N它们是其整体低压线束系统的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.78,0:44:47.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, no no composite dash, but realistically, I do have a picture of this in a second.\N所以，没有复合仪表盘，但说实话，我马上就能拿出这张图。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:47.86,0:44:48.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,They've pushed almost all that content,\N他们几乎推送了所有这些内容，
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.46,0:44:51.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,um forward of essentially the the cab dash panel,\N向前看基本上就是仪表盘面板，
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.41,0:44:56.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,which I do think is noteworthy as far as when you were to actually pop the\N这在我看来值得注意，因为当你真正启动时
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.78,0:45:01.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,hood on this, when you look at this here and in relation to where the cab is,\N把 hood 放上，你看这里，和驾驶室的位置相对比的话，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:01.82,0:45:07.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,it sets everything up like all of these um like service and essentially like\N它把一切都设置好，就像所有这些服务一样，本质上是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.26,0:45:09.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,pre-service and like um fluid like caps and reservoirs,\N服务前和类似液体的储液罐及油箱，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.82,0:45:17.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,and they off to the side they also had essentially the light bar and the washer um bottle assembly. All of that is\N而且在旁边，他们还配有灯条和雨刷水壶组件。所有这些都
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.06,0:45:22.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,essentially right at, you know, waist level. It's all consolidated in one area, and it sits roughly here.\N基本上就在腰部高度左右，所有东西都集中在一个区域，大概就在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.22,0:45:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it's just another thing that was kind of noteworthy is,\N所以，另一件值得一提的事是，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:25.18,0:45:29.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, from an owner-operator and just a user perspective, you know, most of things that you're checking cuz\N从所有者兼运营者以及普通用户的角度来看，你所检查的大多数事情，其实
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.62,0:45:33.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're not checking nearly as much as a traditional truck, all is located here.\N你检查的远少于传统卡车，所有信息都集中在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.86,0:45:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can essentially pop, take a look, and then see anything else. Like,\N你基本上可以随手一拿，看看，然后就能发现其他东西。比如，
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.78,0:45:44.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,everything that is high cost or um I would say com- complex from the the\N所有高成本或我说的复杂的东西
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.70,0:45:46.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,the thermal system is all pretty much in plain view um to\N散热系统基本上全都一目了然。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.68,0:45:51.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,both the the operator or anyone doing service on it. So, we\N无论是操作人员还是任何对其进行维护的人。所以，我们
Dialogue: 0,0:45:51.70,0:45:52.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,just finished up the Tesla Semi tour.\N刚结束特斯拉半挂卡车的参观之旅。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:52.46,0:45:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Honestly, it's exactly kind of what I expected to see. Uh super impressed as far as like the automation, the\N说实话，这完全符合我的预期。说实话，自动化方面真的让我印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.14,0:46:03.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,challenge of certain things. Like, you know, we'd heard and there's materials about the essentially just the powder\N某些事物的挑战。比如，我们之前听说过，关于那些基本上只是粉末的材料
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.26,0:46:04.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,coating, but you know, they're not e-coating, not doing anything.\N涂层，但你知道，他们不是电泳涂层，什么都没做。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.97,0:46:08.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're absolutely challenging their requirements as far as like the body\N他们正完全在挑战自身对机体的要求
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.50,0:46:12.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,structure. Um so, the things they're doing there, I would argue no one else is doing in industry.\N结构方面，我认为他们在那里所做的事情，业界其他公司无人能及。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.98,0:46:16.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um when we were going through and looking at essentially the chassis components, I mean,\N嗯，当我们查看底盘部件时，我的意思是，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.79,0:46:19.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,as much that is non-handed as possible. So, lower\N尽可能减少非手控的部分。因此，更低
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.62,0:46:24.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,control arms, upper I don't know for sure, but you look at lower control arms, upper control arms, knuckles. So,\N控制臂，上控制臂我不太确定，但你看下控制臂、上控制臂、转向节。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.22,0:46:28.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,they they just tweak essentially their steering arm interface and bolt that on.\N他们只是简单地调整一下转向臂的接口，然后直接装上去。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.14,0:46:28.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everything else like it's non-handed.\N其他所有东西都像非右手的那样。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.98,0:46:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You just look at essentially the castings and what they're doing to join them like the front cradle itself.\N你只需看看那些铸件，以及它们是如何连接的，比如前摇臂本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.10,0:46:40.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Honestly, most of the vehicle is kind of what I would love to see scaled down in maybe like a body-on-frame truck\N说实话，这辆车的大部分我其实都希望能在类似底盘式卡车的车型上缩小规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.42,0:46:42.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,personally. Um but, it's impressive as far as I'm concerned as far as serviceability.\N就我而言，说实话，它的可维护性确实令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.99,0:46:46.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you look at the packs, where it's integrated and where\N当你看这些模块时，它们的集成位置在哪里，以及
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.58,0:46:47.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,there is like a high level of integration,\N存在高度的集成。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:47.98,0:46:53.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,where there is um deliberate separation of components and assemblies for serviceability.\N其中，为了便于维护，组件和总成被刻意分开。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.17,0:46:53.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean,\N我的意思是，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.59,0:46:54.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's clear when you look through stuff,\N看东西时，这一点很明显，
Dialogue: 0,0:46:54.94,0:46:59.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's a lot of consolidation, but there's a lot of forethought as far as how you need to service things to ensure\N有很多整合，但同时也需要深思熟虑，以确保能够妥善服务各项需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.82,0:47:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,it has a uh a long life. But, honestly,\N它寿命很长。但说实话，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.46,0:47:04.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh very impressive from what we saw. Even just the IP line behind me,\N嗯，非常令人印象深刻，仅看我身后的IP线路就已如此出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.56,0:47:07.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,which you can see. We can't go any farther back,\N你看到了，我们无法再往前推进了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:07.86,0:47:13.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it looks like it's 12 stations. You can see one a series of castings as it comes here. There's um\N但看起来有12个工位。你可以看到一连串铸件从这里过来。嗯
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.42,0:47:16.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a not another if you can see line side, right? So,\N如果你能看到侧面的话，那就没有别的了，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:16.12,0:47:21.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,that is a top essentially carrier coupled with essentially probably vibe welded, you\N那基本上是一个顶部的载流子，几乎可能是通过振动焊接连接的。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.54,0:47:26.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,know, HVAC ducts that are clam shell in this out as it comes around the lower parts, the upper trim level, then it\N知道，空调风管在下部绕到上部饰板时呈贝壳状，然后向上延伸到上部饰板级别。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.42,0:47:28.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of moves its way around. So, like even the IP,\N有点像在四处移动。比如就连IP也一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:28.27,0:47:32.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,extremely extremely simple as far as how it's overall built up is,\N整体构建方式极其极其简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.90,0:47:36.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you can kind of see that throughout the entire truck itself.\N你几乎能从整辆卡车的各个部分都看出这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:36.74,0:47:41.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then as we finish the tour, this is off the left-hand side. Um and for a past project, I did a lot of work in\N然后参观结束时，这里在左侧。嗯，之前的一个项目中，我做了大量相关工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.62,0:47:42.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,IPs,\NIP 地址
Dialogue: 0,0:47:42.86,0:47:46.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,um more specifically like the structure and getting some complexity out. So, I ran off,\N更具体地说，是结构上的调整，以及去除一些复杂性。于是，我便开始行动了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.23,0:47:49.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,got some pictures of this. We couldn't walk in here, uh unfortunately,\N拍了一些照片。很遗憾，我们没法走进来。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:49.94,0:47:54.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,but um I was going to say, I don't remember this part.\N不过呃，我想说，我不记得这一部分了。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.62,0:47:55.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah. I went rogue. Um so,\N对，对，我擅自行动了。呃，所以……
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.42,0:48:00.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,um I and our Tesla handler kind of got me back under control. But, um,\N呃，我和特斯拉的负责人把我重新控制住了。不过，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.50,0:48:04.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,overall, when you when you look at the essentially the stations, I think there's roughly 12.\N总的来说，当你看这些站点时，我认为大约有12个。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.50,0:48:07.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a little difficult to see with some of the\N有些地方看不太清楚
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.10,0:48:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,pylons. A pretty simple IP build-up. Um, the the setup itself is simple. But,\N电塔。一个相当简单的IP搭建。嗯，这个设置本身很简单。但是，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.42,0:48:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,here is a great image, and honestly, it's like a perfect, um, it's halfway through the build-up of the the IP line.\N这是一张很棒的图片，说实话，它就像一个完美的……嗯，正处于IP线路构建的中途。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:16.14,0:48:22.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, to get to see the steering column in place, you can see a little bit of the the, um, cross car beam substrate\N但要看到转向柱就位的情况，你能看到一点横向车梁的基板
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.02,0:48:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,come, um, coming through itself. So, each of the screen provisions are here.\N过来，呃，它自己过来了。所以，每个屏幕的配置都在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:26.22,0:48:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um,\N嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.78,0:48:29.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then essentially, it's difficult to kind of see how much is\N然后本质上，很难看出其中有多少是
Dialogue: 0,0:48:29.94,0:48:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,separate as it kind of comes down the line. But, um,\N分开，因为它会沿着生产线下来。不过，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.02,0:48:38.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, one thing that's what really spoke to me is, um,\N你知道吗，有一件事真正打动了我，就是，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.58,0:48:44.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's a fair amount of line side space here, and there's not a lot of complexity, right? So, they they are\N这里有不少机柜侧边空间，而且复杂度也不高，对吧？所以，他们……
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.30,0:48:47.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,building, you know, this is a smaller line from what I have seen just in general.\N建造方面，你知道，这比我平时看到的要短一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:47.38,0:48:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, but there's essentially no other parts here. There's\N嗯，这里基本上没有其他部件了。没有
Dialogue: 0,0:48:50.94,0:48:54.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think one flavor of cross car beam that you're getting in this in comparison to uh,\N我认为，与你之前所见相比，这种跨车梁的某种类型呈现出不同的特点。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.63,0:48:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of their other vehicles or just in general in an\N他们其他车辆，或者一般情况下
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.98,0:49:03.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,industry where, you know, you may swap these lower trim panels out with the door cards based off of a trim level or\N在汽车制造行业，你可以根据不同的配置等级，将低配的门板饰条更换为门卡饰板。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.06,0:49:04.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,anything like that. Um, so, it is pretty small for kind\N类似的东西。嗯，所以，就种类而言，它相当小。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:04.85,0:49:08.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,of what appears to be essentially complete build-up and prep\N看起来几乎已经完全建成并准备就绪
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.94,0:49:13.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,for installation to the vehicle. But, you can see, um,\N用于安装到车辆上。但你看，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.10,0:49:15.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, part of the the structure in the sled, but more is uh,\N你知道，雪橇结构的一部分，但更多的是……
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.72,0:49:18.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,for the HVAC kind of coming through here, where it's\N对于这种通过这里的暖通空调系统来说
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.02,0:49:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,going to receive whatever the actual main HVAC system on the far side of the dash uh, panel is going to provide\N将接收仪表盘另一侧实际主暖通空调系统所提供的空调风量。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.74,0:49:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,for the demisters and essentially your normal vents. Um,\N用于除雾器，以及普通的出风口。嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.18,0:49:32.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,but this is kind of superimposed uh, a little bit bigger here,\N但这个有点叠加，这里稍微大一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.27,0:49:35.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you can see here, uh, the majority of this is all\N但你看这里，呃，大部分都是
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.70,0:49:37.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,castings.\N铸件。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.86,0:49:43.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, what I think is noteworthy is, you know, the first Tesla we ever saw,\N嗯，我觉得值得注意的是，我们第一次看到的那辆特斯拉，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.86,0:49:47.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think was stamp steel and tube uh, structure for the cross car beam. Then,\N我认为是用于横向车梁的钢和管材结构。然后，
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.86,0:49:50.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,we saw the migration to essentially a lot of aluminum extrusions\N我们看到，实际上大量采用了铝挤压工艺。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:50.58,0:49:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,and stampings in some of the early, later, I guess,\N以及一些早期和后期的冲压件，我想
Dialogue: 0,0:49:54.50,0:49:57.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, early Model X and the later Model S's.\N呃，早期的 Model X 和后期的 Model S。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.34,0:50:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then we saw the transition. I don't know if you can see it off to the side here to the clinger style beam.\N然后我们看到了过渡。我不知道你们能不能看到这边的附着式梁结构。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:03.98,0:50:09.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh Eric's not paying attention. But um which is essentially a formed aluminum tube with some knurling and it's shot\N呃，埃里克没在注意。但这个本质上是一个带一些滚花的成型铝管，然后被射出去了。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:09.82,0:50:12.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,over in a composite material.\N另一边是复合材料。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.22,0:50:18.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in our Model S and then subsequently every Tesla that we have seen since then, um\N然后在我们的 Model S 以及之后我们看到的每一辆特斯拉上，嗯
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.06,0:50:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's been an iteration of that to kind of get out of that\N这已经是一次迭代，以摆脱那种状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.86,0:50:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,style beam and maybe even some of the IP associated with it.\N风格光束，甚至可能还包括与之相关的部分知识产权。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:23.70,0:50:29.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and they do essentially galvanize stamping and they shoot over it with a a high gloss fill.\N嗯，它们实际上会进行电镀冲压，然后在其上喷涂高光填充层。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.54,0:50:30.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so we were being the next Tesla vehicle,\N所以我们正成为下一代特斯拉车型，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:30.43,0:50:34.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,we were excited to see if we would continue or we or where essentially\N我们很兴奋地想看看我们是否还能继续，或者究竟会怎样。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:34.74,0:50:36.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,what strategy they would\N他们会选择什么策略
Dialogue: 0,0:50:36.22,0:50:41.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,use. Um seeing essentially an entire cast structure doesn't necessarily surprise me.\N嗯，看到整个结构框架其实并不让我感到意外。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.44,0:50:43.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think when you look at this truck\N我觉得当你看这辆卡车时
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.02,0:50:47.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,in comparison to any other vehicle they've ever built. Um with the two large screens on either side,\N与其他任何他们曾制造过的车型相比，这款车型两侧配有两块大型屏幕。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.97,0:50:50.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,the fact that you can walk around in the truck,\N你可以在卡车里走动的事实，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.78,0:50:52.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,like when you grab a and I don't want to abuse it,\N就像你拿起一个时，我不想滥用它，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.78,0:50:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like I shook the shook the screens and I mean they're they're\N但我晃了晃屏幕，我的意思是，它们真的在晃
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.30,0:51:04.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,pretty securely mounted. So um I think that would drive a lot of load cases, you know, into\N安装得相当牢固。所以我觉得这会引发很多载荷工况，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.50,0:51:06.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,the um the beam itself. Being a center steer vehicle as well,\N呃，这个光束本身。它也是中轴转向的车辆。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:06.11,0:51:10.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,like right in the center, it doesn't even have essentially\N就在正中央，它甚至基本上没有
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.30,0:51:15.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,a hinge pillar or a pedal box to kind of help it out on that one side of the vehicle. Um so everything is a lot of\N一个铰链支柱或踏板盒，来帮助支撑车辆那一侧。所以一切都变得轻松多了。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.34,0:51:22.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that those loads are running in the center. It makes sense to me to see it being a casting. I don't know if it's\N这些负载正在中心运行，我觉得这样看就像在铸造一样。我不确定是不是
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.06,0:51:27.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,mag or aluminum. It kind of looks like it might be a mixture of both. Um from what I can see here.\N镁或铝，看起来像是两者的混合物。根据我所看到的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.46,0:51:32.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But one thing that's interesting is you can see all the scalloping here. It's multiple pieces.\N但有趣的是，你可以看到这里的波浪状纹路，这是由多个部分组成的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.42,0:51:37.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um again, to me that makes sense. It kind of goes to the earlier point of shipping air. This is a large assembly.\N嗯，再次强调，这对我来说是有道理的。这其实呼应了之前提到的“运输空气”的观点。这是一个大型组件。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:37.70,0:51:43.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of the biggest advantage of a kind of a clinger style beam is you bring in small tubes, high rack density, you\N一种夹持式梁结构最大的优势在于，你可以接入细小的管道，实现高机架密度。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:43.46,0:51:48.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,unload them, shoot over them, and then send them to the IP line for build up.\N卸下它们，射向它们，然后发送到IP线进行组装。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.74,0:51:53.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So um where a conventional steel IP beam a a lot lower rack density\N所以，传统的钢制IP梁，机架密度要低得多
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.50,0:51:59.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,a lot more trips with a truck um and just in general a little bit more of a logistics tail to that.\N更多的卡车运输，以及整体上物流需求稍微多一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:59.10,0:52:02.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but when you look at this I don't know how many separate castings per se it is,\N但你看这个，我不确定具体有多少个独立的铸件。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.53,0:52:06.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it probably is like somewhere between six to eight, but you\N但可能大概在六到八之间，不过你
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.46,0:52:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,look at where the structure is and you know, just die draw alone it kind of makes sense that they broke it all up\N看看这个结构，你就会发现，仅仅从设计上来看，它们把所有部分拆开也合情合理。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.42,0:52:13.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,for the the the functional needs that they needed.\N他们所需的功能需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:13.66,0:52:16.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not sure if they're made in a family tool or anything like that,\N我不确定它们是不是用家庭工具之类的做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:16.89,0:52:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,but um it doesn't necessarily surprise me to see\N但说实话，看到这一幕我并不觉得意外
Dialogue: 0,0:52:19.90,0:52:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,this um as a strategy that they chose for this vehicle. Um I was kind of expecting to see um more composites\N这个嘛，是他们为这款车型选择的一种策略。我本来还期待能看到更多复合材料。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.10,0:52:32.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,used, but in all honesty just given the nature of this vehicle, its service life that that makes sense to me. So.\N虽然用了，但说实话，考虑到这款车的特性，它的使用年限也说得过去。所以。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.40,0:52:37.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, um overall, like I said, there is a ton to deep dive.\N你知道，总的来说，就像我说的，有很多内容值得深入探讨。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:37.52,0:52:40.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could probably go through all this, get Carl talk\N我们或许可以过一遍这些内容，让卡尔来谈一谈
Dialogue: 0,0:52:40.90,0:52:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,through this for another couple hours and that's kind of the intent. Um I was excited to see this.\N再这样持续几个小时，这正是设计的初衷。嗯，看到这个我真的很兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.86,0:52:50.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um Honestly, the biggest thing like when people are asking me kind\N说实话，人们问我最多的问题就是这个
Dialogue: 0,0:52:50.84,0:52:55.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,of what I expected or what I thought of it um\N和我预期的或我原本想的不一样啊
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.10,0:53:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,the compromises that I saw here between integration and serviceability I think is telling and for me\N我在这里看到的集成与可维护性之间的权衡，我认为很有启发性，对我而言是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.94,0:53:01.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,interesting.\N有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.90,0:53:05.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's you know, one of my favorite words. Um what I'd like to see,\N而且你知道，这是我最喜欢的词之一。嗯，我想看到的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.23,0:53:08.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm curious about is you know, they got a vehicle that can\N我很好奇的是，你们知道，他们有一辆能跑的车
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.74,0:53:12.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,tow 11,000 lb and they have a vehicle that can tow 80,000 lb.\N牵引力11,000磅，而他们有一辆能牵引80,000磅的车辆。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.25,0:53:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think they now know how a body on frame with the rigid\N我认为他们现在明白了一体式车身与刚性框架的区别。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.02,0:53:19.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,mounted battery works over a long period of time with a lot of miles.\N电池长时间运行，行驶里程很长。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:19.20,0:53:22.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do they decide to build something that's kind of\N他们决定打造一些类似的东西吗
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.66,0:53:28.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,in that half-ton to one-ton range towing, you know,\N那个半吨到一吨的拖拽范围，你知道的，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:28.62,0:53:33.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,somewhere between 12,000 and 35,000 lb and can and competing essentially with\N介于12,000到35,000磅之间，且几乎与之竞争
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.46,0:53:37.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,um you know, the breadbasket of of your kind of heavy-duty trucks.\N你知道的，这可是你们这类重型卡车的粮仓。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.30,0:53:39.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um that's in some ways what I'm most excited about. Aesthetically,\N从某种角度来看，这正是我最兴奋的地方。从审美上来说，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.83,0:53:42.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not a big Cybertruck fan. Um I think it works\N我不是特斯拉 Cybertruck 的粉丝。呃，我觉得它其实挺合适的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.02,0:53:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,for a lot of people but um I think when I look at what they did here and the decisions made it it really\N对很多人来说是这样，但我觉得，当我看到他们在这里所做的一切以及做出的决策时，真的
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.26,0:53:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,makes me excited for something they could do along the line and that kind of work truck realm.\N让我对他们在这一领域，尤其是这类工程卡车方面的潜力感到兴奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:55.90,0:53:58.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,We'll just have to see but we're looking forward to kind of\N我们只能拭目以待了，但我们很期待接下来的发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.04,0:54:01.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,deep diving this a little bit more with you guys and just\N再深入和大家探讨一下这个问题
Dialogue: 0,0:54:01.54,0:54:05.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,going through because I think there is a lot to unpack here with the\N因为我觉得这里有很多值得深入探讨的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:54:05.30,0:54:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,truck and frankly I could see why I'd love to see an early\N卡车，说实话，我明白为什么了，真想早点看到。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.42,0:54:13.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,version but I can see why in some ways it took so long right it's a very different vehicle it's one of the things\N但我觉得在某些方面，它花了这么长时间也情有可原，毕竟这是一辆非常不同的车。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.90,0:54:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,they kept stressing right it's like you're talking something that is being loaded at 100% duty cycles almost his\N他们反复强调，这就像设备几乎以100%的负载率在运行一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.58,0:54:25.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,entire life it's just different than essentially a passenger vehicle so\N整个生命周期都与普通乘用车截然不同
Dialogue: 0,0:54:25.54,0:54:25.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,thank you and stay tuned.\N谢谢观看，敬请期待。
